1
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,119
Esenbike..

2
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:31,719
You see the situation Ulugan is in.

3
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:35,639
His fate...

4
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:40,319
...is not just the price of what he has done.

5
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:42,839
It is also...

6
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,679
...a lesson for those...

7
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:46,839
...who walk on the same path with him.

8
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,559
Osman!

9
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:58,439
Do you think there won't be a
price for this insolence and insult?

10
00:02:59,640 --> 00:03:00,479
Alps!

11
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,719
Mother..

12
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,759
They have more men than we do.

13
00:03:16,640 --> 00:03:20,639
So you are saying you planned
your trap long ago, Osman, huh?

14
00:03:22,920 --> 00:03:26,319
When I die here like a hero...

15
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:29,319
...your fate... -Shut up

16
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,559
Shut up!

17
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,839
May your word be as short as your life!

18
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:35,039
Like a flooding river...

19
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,039
...the furor that will rain on the frontiers...

20
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,239
...will drown you with its anger.

21
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:43,599
Sea, huh?

22
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:44,879
Sea?

23
00:03:46,040 --> 00:03:48,119
I will shed your dirty blood...

24
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:51,999
...and I will stain the sea with that blood.

25
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:56,839
I will make endless mountains
out of your severed heads.

26
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,839
You will see what nursing a grudge...

27
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:06,719
..costs here.

28
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:07,759
All of you!

29
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,439
My Bey!

30
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:21,599
Protect Osman Bey!

31
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,879
I am here, Ulugan!

32
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:34,159
Where do you think you are running? Where?

33
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,199
Shields! -Move!

34
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:40,639
Clear!

35
00:04:50,640 --> 00:04:51,679
Clear!

36
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:53,879
Move!

37
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:56,239
Alps! Attack!

38
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:01,319
Walk nokers! Come on!

39
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:48,439
Alps!

40
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:50,879
Turn this place into hell for them!

41
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:52,239
Come on!

42
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,759
Come on, open the door!

43
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,839
Bala.

44
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:01,439
You need me.

45
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:04,319
You will never be able to find Halime.

46
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,519
Hold the exits.

47
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:07,999
Soldiers!

48
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:14,039
Attack!

49
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:36,359
My Shahzade, the door is open!

50
00:06:36,400 --> 00:06:37,999
Next time...

51
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,799
Soldiers!

52
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:44,839
Take the Priestess!

53
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:57,199
Mother... The door is open! Come on!

54
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:05,079
-Come on! Come on!
-Come on!

55
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:06,799
Come on! Come on!

56
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:09,359
Damn it!

57
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:10,559
Here... Get in.

58
00:07:16,840 --> 00:07:19,479
Wait... Wait... -Come.

59
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:20,679
I have it.

60
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:22,279
Are you alright?

61
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,159
Leave me here.

62
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,959
I will slow you down.

63
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,839
Go, Bala Hatun.

64
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:30,399
You are the key that will
take me to my daughter.

65
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,159
We will not leave you here.

66
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:36,519
You kept coming to the frontiers!

67
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:39,879
Which one of you escaped the
Turks' swords, huh? Which one?

68
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:44,399
Ulugan!

69
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:45,159
Esenbike!

70
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:49,399
You will die soon.

71
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:52,639
You, whose state I have crushed under my feet...

72
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:55,119
...think I am powerless huh?

73
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:33,719
Ulugan! I am here Ulugan! Get up!

74
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:35,639
You will recover! Come on! Come.

75
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:39,558
Come! You will recover for our revenge! Come on!

76
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,199
Come on nokers!

77
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,439
Attack!

78
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:05,999
My Bey! Ulugan is running away!

79
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:15,839
Boran!

80
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,999
Cerkutay!

81
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,719
Go after them!

82
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:19,959
As you order, my Bey!

83
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,359
Brother..

84
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,159
We need to kill these first.

85
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:35,679
Come on!

86
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,319
Come on.

87
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:56,319
Mother, we are losing our nokers one by one.

88
00:09:56,320 --> 00:10:00,479
We must not be overwhelmed by
our ambition and die in Osman's trap.

89
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:03,439
The battle has just begun, Osman.

90
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,559
We'll meet again.

91
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:11,999
Nokers will stay behind us and protect us.

92
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:12,999
We are leaving.

93
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:14,199
Come on.

94
00:10:17,600 --> 00:10:20,159
Alps! Beys!

95
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:24,679
First, we will crush the
snake's tail, then its head.

96
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:36,719
Open the door!

97
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,719
Mother! This door cannot hold much longer.

98
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:42,079
We need to leave this place now! Come on!

99
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:45,079
Come on! Hurry up! This way

100
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,919
Come on! -Leave now!

101
00:10:47,040 --> 00:10:49,359
Come on! Leave!

102
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,999
Come on

103
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,919
Come on, come on.

104
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,959
-Hurry!
-Help!

105
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,279
They've broken the door and are coming.

106
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:20,119
Gulce, give me the flying flame.

107
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:31,159
Light... The door.. This
way! We have to go this way.

108
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,279
Alaaddin.
-You go!

109
00:11:34,680 --> 00:11:37,479
-Mother.
-Mother, come on.

110
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:40,519
Hold on.

111
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:52,519
Come to me.

112
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:55,199
Come to me, you dogs.

113
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:58,999
O Allah.

114
00:12:04,720 --> 00:12:06,519
Soldiers, stop

115
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:22,759
Esenbike must have left watchmen behind.

116
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:24,759
Kanyumaz!
-My Bey.

117
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:28,519
-Follow them.
-As you order, my Bey.

118
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:31,719
Won't we go after them, my Bey?
-No.

119
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:37,399
She must have got out of the forest by now.

120
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:39,599
We can't catch even if we

121
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,199
My Bey.

122
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:46,279
My Bey, Ulugan has escaped.

123
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:48,959
They left the carriage somewhere in the woods.

124
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,599
And they moved on foot.

125
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,639
We couldn't trace.

126
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:58,079
Altuga is as good at hiding
the traces as I'm good at tracing.

127
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:04,719
I opened such a sword wound in his chest...

128
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:06,839
...he can't go far away.

129
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,719
He'll come out sooner or later.

130
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:14,079
We're going to our tribe.

131
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:18,039
We'll have a council and set the target.

132
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,679
Beys.

133
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:22,679
You are coming with us.

134
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,119
Let's go.

135
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:30,719
Hold on.

136
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,479
Mother.
-Yes?

137
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:36,039
We got one step closer to Halime.

138
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:39,239
Thanks to Allah. We found
out my daughter's name.

139
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:42,777
We'll find more, mother.
You'll be together soon.

140
00:13:42,789 --> 00:13:43,759
God willing.

141
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,479
Kismet, prepare the disguises.

142
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:51,839
Sofia will come after us. We should
give Osman Bey the great news.

143
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:53,759
Alaaddin, let's go!

144
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:04,439
That woman has to die before she speaks, Hristo.

145
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:06,599
She told Bala Poena's name.

146
00:14:06,600 --> 00:14:09,599
If we can't catch them,
she will tell her everything.

147
00:14:09,720 --> 00:14:11,159
Let's go faster.

148
00:14:11,320 --> 00:14:14,007
We have to find them
before they arrive in the tribe.

149
00:14:14,019 --> 00:14:14,919
Let's go!

150
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:48,599
I told you. Osman is like no other enemies.

151
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,799
He plans every detail.

152
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:57,879
It seems you admire Osman a lot.

153
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:05,319
You should know I'm like
no other enemies either.

154
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:13,119
Many like Osman died under my feet.

155
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:18,279
I'm only praying for Allah
to take Osman's life tonight.

156
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:20,479
I have no other thoughts.

157
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:25,399
That's what is going to happen, Begum Hatun.

158
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:31,759
Osman is going to pass away tonight
at his most defenseless moment.

159
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:35,559
Osman isn't going to carry a sword tonight.

160
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:38,679
Tonight is the best time to kill him.

161
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:43,799
He should thank us. We're
going to kill him at Qadr night.

162
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:02,599
Tell alps to provide tighter
security around the tribe.

163
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,039
Sure, my Bey.

164
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:08,119
Host the Beys until the council
starts. Tell Sahin Bey to come.

165
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:11,079
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

166
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:16,319
This way, Beys.
This way, please.

167
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:18,519
Welcome, father.

168
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:23,559
-Where is your mother, my dear?
-We were waiting for them.

169
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,959
I hope they aren't in trouble, father.

170
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:27,999
What if that demon tricked them?

171
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:31,319
No, my dear. We know about all their tricks.

172
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:34,839
Maybe, they are coming back with good news, huh?

173
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:38,519
-God willing.
-God willing, God willing.

174
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,719
Poena!

175
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:46,239
Poena!

176
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:49,479
Bala!

177
00:16:53,400 --> 00:16:54,879
What's going on, Bala?

178
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:57,439
They named our daughter Poena, my Bey.

179
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,479
What?

180
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:03,439
-How? Where is she?
-We'll know everything, my Bey.

181
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:08,439
Take her to the healing tent!
Cauterize her wound carefully, sisters!

182
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:15,398
Lucia.

183
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,318
-Who is she? -Priestess Lucia.

184
00:17:17,319 --> 00:17:20,999
Just as she was about to speak,
Sofia arrived and tried to kill her.

185
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,559
Sofia... Demon

186
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:28,919
Although she's trying to keep our daughter
away, she's bringing her closer to us!

187
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:36,039
Don't worry. Very soon.

188
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,679
-Very soon.
-Yes.

189
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:48,999
-My Hatun.
-My Bey.

190
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:53,599
Are you going to battles
even though you are pregnant?

191
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:57,639
If you don't take me with you, I go with mother.

192
00:17:58,120 --> 00:18:00,199
Besides, my baby is pleased with this.

193
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:03,319
Well... He's like his father, huh?

194
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:06,479
-Yes.
-Of course, yes.

195
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,559
Come on, let's go.

196
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:34,039
Tengri (Turkish-Mongolian God)
will heal you, Ulugan.

197
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:49,279
Your soul will be purified from the death.

198
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,639
You'll repel the dark spirits...

199
00:19:10,840 --> 00:19:13,279
...and heal Ulugan, Shaman.

200
00:19:13,880 --> 00:19:18,039
Otherwise, I won't let you live.

201
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:21,959
His armor saved his life. He's going to recover.

202
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:25,399
Yet..

203
00:19:26,120 --> 00:19:29,479
...dark spirits want him, Altuga.

204
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:40,439
Then repel those spirits, Shaman.

205
00:19:53,080 --> 00:20:00,239
Ulugan! Ulugan! Ulugan!

206
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:05,119
Ulugan is reborn every day!

207
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:07,439
Wake up for vengenace, Ulugan!

208
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:16,719
Wake up for vengenace, Ulugan!

209
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:48,279
She's the priestess who looked
after our daughter for years, huh?

210
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,015
She's the witness of
the years they stole from us.

211
00:20:52,027 --> 00:20:54,599
She knows everything
we want to know, my Bey.

212
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:59,879
Alaaddin, help her recover somehow, son.

213
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:02,599
I'll do my best, father.

214
00:21:02,800 --> 00:21:06,079
We'll help her live, with Allah's will.

215
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:08,759
-God willing. God willing.
-God willing.

216
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:13,559
Is your daughter's name Poena?

217
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,959
The priestess was going
to tell us everything, but...

218
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:21,679
But the snake Sofia didn't let her.

219
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:23,879
What's that supposed to mean?

220
00:21:24,080 --> 00:21:26,919
Lucia, why did you do such a thing?

221
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,639
Why did you give my name?

222
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:33,119
Her name isn't Poena but Halime.

223
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:38,119
They made my sister
forget us and everything else.

224
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:42,159
Whatever they did to her mind,

225
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:47,519
...she has our soul and our blood.

226
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:51,359
They can never change her.

227
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:53,639
Don't be worrying.

228
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:55,559
Right.

229
00:21:55,960 --> 00:22:00,559
When we come back together, we
will help her remember everything.

230
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:04,279
Tell Ulgen to prepare sherbet.

231
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:07,199
She needs to regain strength.

232
00:22:11,760 --> 00:22:14,799
Bala, let's go.

233
00:22:16,680 --> 00:22:18,159
-Son.
My Bey.

234
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,779
Let's go, Bala.

235
00:22:22,214 --> 00:22:25,324
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

236
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:35,039
-Alaaddin Bey.
-Yes?

237
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:37,559
How can a person even forget?

238
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:40,319
They said..

239
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:42,799
Halime can't remember.

240
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:47,639
Those who want to do evil things
may find many ways, Meryem.

241
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:54,439
Is it possible to forget everything?

242
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,959
It's possible.

243
00:22:58,200 --> 00:23:01,039
Of course, it is. I once heard in the madrasah.

244
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:03,239
But I've never seen it.

245
00:23:11,520 --> 00:23:13,839
They play with the mind, Meryem.

246
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:18,719
There are many poisons in the nature.

247
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:21,359
But not all of them kill.

248
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:23,799
They make you lose your mind.

249
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:26,119
Did you drink the syrup?

250
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:28,519
No, it got broken before I could drink.

251
00:23:29,840 --> 00:23:31,879
Damn it, Poena.

252
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:35,119
Here. Don't forget to take.

253
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:37,479
Keep it carefully.

254
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:41,959
The syrup bottles.

255
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,679
Yes.

256
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,359
You're right, Meryem.

257
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:50,719
Praise be, you're very smart.

258
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,919
I couldn't think of that.

259
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:57,599
Let me go check them.

260
00:24:12,160 --> 00:24:13,999
Am I...

261
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:17,039
Am I Halime?

262
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:23,119
Aykut Cavus, tell the dervishes...

263
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:25,759
...to be my guests at Qadr night.

264
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:27,119
As you order, my Bey.

265
00:24:27,520 --> 00:24:31,639
-You tell Beys to come to my tent.
-As you order, my Bey.

266
00:24:36,640 --> 00:24:39,999
Mother Sultan, I insist.

267
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:43,439
We should wait no longer.

268
00:24:43,720 --> 00:24:47,399
We should slaughter Osman's people tonight.

269
00:24:47,960 --> 00:24:51,599
-He already deserved this.
-That would be great.

270
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:54,399
If we slaughter people now.

271
00:24:55,000 --> 00:25:00,599
...not only Kayi people but also all the
Muslims in the frontiers will rise against us.

272
00:25:00,720 --> 00:25:03,359
We have enough power to make them all kneel.

273
00:25:03,520 --> 00:25:07,439
What are we waiting for? Will
we let Osman get stronger?

274
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:09,359
Never.

275
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:11,839
The day after tomorrow

276
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:16,159
...even Osman's name will
be wiped out of these lands.

277
00:25:16,520 --> 00:25:19,559
I will do such thing...

278
00:25:20,600 --> 00:25:23,799
-Do I have permission?
-Come in, Altuga.

279
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:31,319
I've brought Ulugan. He's in the healing tent.

280
00:25:31,840 --> 00:25:34,599
Shaman says he's recovering fast.

281
00:25:35,400 --> 00:25:37,039
Good.

282
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:42,839
That means we will do away with Osman together.

283
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:46,879
The traps set against Turks...

284
00:25:49,280 --> 00:25:53,799
Those who do their best to separate us...

285
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:56,519
You know how treacherous...

286
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:58,879
...how sinister...

287
00:26:00,760 --> 00:26:02,799
...they are.

288
00:26:03,600 --> 00:26:07,479
You showed us the evil disguised
as goodness, Osman Bey.

289
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:08,879
Thank you.

290
00:26:09,840 --> 00:26:14,839
This foresight will bring Kayi back
to its old days, Allah knows the best.

291
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:17,039
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

292
00:26:19,680 --> 00:26:22,639
The punches we have
thrown at the infidels so far...

293
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:24,879
...have surprised them greatly.

294
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:29,119
...only one final punch...

295
00:26:29,720 --> 00:26:31,279
...remains.

296
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:34,399
My Bey, give us the order and we will kill them.

297
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:37,319
No, not while our hands are in the air.

298
00:26:37,480 --> 00:26:40,919
They will understand when
the punch pierces their chest.

299
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:45,199
Until then, we will make our moves secretly.

300
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:50,359
The last move before
we rise against the infidels.

301
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:53,999
Our troops and the Alps of the Turkmen Beys...

302
00:26:54,640 --> 00:26:56,239
...will unite in the quarters.

303
00:26:57,600 --> 00:26:58,959
Together...

304
00:27:00,040 --> 00:27:02,039
...we will become one army.

305
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:06,639
Each of our tribes is in a
different place around the frontier.

306
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:11,479
Gathering our troops in the quarters without
the Mongols noticing will be very difficult.

307
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:16,879
Of course, freedom is not
something easily gained.

308
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:20,719
Of course, it will be difficult.

309
00:27:22,800 --> 00:27:24,919
If the issue is the Turk's
struggle for freedom...

310
00:27:25,280 --> 00:27:28,799
...the Beys will do their duty
without any mistakes, my Bey.

311
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:30,959
You just order us, my Bey.

312
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:34,959
Death on this path is the
most honorable fate for us.

313
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:38,639
Orhan, tell your bravest Alps to set out.

314
00:27:39,680 --> 00:27:44,759
The Sivrioyuk location, which is
far from us but close to the infidels.

315
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:49,039
We will set up our secret quarters there.

316
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:50,639
As you order my Bey.

317
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:53,399
While we unite in the quarters...

318
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:55,879
...we will become one army.

319
00:27:56,840 --> 00:28:00,519
Then, we will take back our tribe.

320
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,719
-God willing, my Bey.
-God willing.

321
00:28:09,040 --> 00:28:10,079
Sargun!

322
00:28:17,320 --> 00:28:20,879
Your anger towards Osman
even burns the ground you step on.

323
00:28:21,520 --> 00:28:23,799
But a chained anger is useless.

324
00:28:25,160 --> 00:28:27,759
I will strangle you..

325
00:28:28,520 --> 00:28:30,079
...with that chain, Ilbay.

326
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:35,159
What do you want?

327
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,239
Osman's lost hopes..

328
00:28:37,400 --> 00:28:38,839
...rise again with faith.

329
00:28:39,400 --> 00:28:41,159
Esenbike is making a mistake.

330
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:45,399
Now is the time to attack and destroy their joy.

331
00:28:47,640 --> 00:28:50,039
Osman.

332
00:28:50,040 --> 00:28:53,039
Osman will drown in his own blood tonight.

333
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:56,439
What about Esenbike?

334
00:28:59,080 --> 00:29:01,279
War has no faith, Ilbay.

335
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:07,119
If necessary, I will get the
allegiance of my enemies with blood.

336
00:29:08,960 --> 00:29:10,919
But I will not let them feel joy.

337
00:29:12,480 --> 00:29:13,519
Sargun.

338
00:29:19,560 --> 00:29:20,879
Let me come with you.

339
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:22,839
I know Osman well.

340
00:29:26,800 --> 00:29:27,839
I know.

341
00:29:29,320 --> 00:29:31,799
You are talented in letting Osman escape.

342
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:35,439
But..

343
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:37,519
But you can be of use to me there.

344
00:29:40,080 --> 00:29:41,119
Get ready.

345
00:29:50,840 --> 00:29:51,879
Ilbay.

346
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:55,439
What is he going to do?

347
00:29:55,440 --> 00:29:57,079
We will kill Osman tonight.

348
00:30:23,880 --> 00:30:25,279
They have removed all the traces.

349
00:30:28,840 --> 00:30:30,119
That doesn't matter.

350
00:30:32,360 --> 00:30:33,919
It doesn't matter.

351
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:39,439
I already know their secret little tribe.

352
00:30:40,080 --> 00:30:41,399
Are we going to raid their tribe?

353
00:30:43,320 --> 00:30:44,359
No.

354
00:30:46,400 --> 00:30:49,359
Osman must have already taken every precaution.

355
00:30:50,840 --> 00:30:53,639
I will go...

356
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:58,519
...and take care of this
matter myself, in silence.

357
00:30:59,840 --> 00:31:01,959
This is very dangerous.

358
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:10,159
Not as dangerous as
letting that fool live, Hristo.

359
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:13,199
I will kill her tonight.

360
00:31:18,480 --> 00:31:19,679
Let's go.

361
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:33,799
I seek refuge with Allah from Satan, the accursed
In the name of Allah, the merciful, the compassionate.

362
00:31:34,120 --> 00:31:40,839
We sent it down on the Night of Glory.

363
00:31:41,080 --> 00:31:46,319
What will explain to you what that Night of Glory is?

364
00:31:46,680 --> 00:31:51,359
The Night of Glory is better than a thousand months;

365
00:31:51,480 --> 00:31:56,938
on that night the angels and the Spirit descend...

366
00:31:56,950 --> 00:32:01,719
again and again with their
Lord’s permission on every task;

367
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:11,039
[there is] peace that night until the break of dawn.

368
00:32:11,230 --> 00:32:14,654
Allah the Almighty said the truth.
Surah Al-Qadr [1-5]

369
00:32:15,304 --> 00:32:32,724
Peace be upon the messengers
and praise be to God the Lord of all the Worlds.

370
00:32:32,832 --> 00:32:33,832
-Surah As-Saffat [181-182]-

371
00:32:34,494 --> 00:32:38,304
Al Fatiha

372
00:32:38,756 --> 00:32:51,576
May Allah's blessings and greetings
be upon Hadrath Muhammed, peace be upon him.

373
00:33:10,400 --> 00:33:11,999
Osman Bey Secret Tents

374
00:33:29,760 --> 00:33:32,119
Come on, let's sit down.

375
00:33:32,280 --> 00:33:34,679
Let's drink some sherbet, huh?

376
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:53,599
Drink, Osman, drink.

377
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:57,479
This will be the last thing you drink.

378
00:38:23,680 --> 00:38:25,079
Attack!

379
00:40:36,040 --> 00:40:37,399
Follow them.

380
00:40:51,480 --> 00:40:53,279
They ran away again, my Bey.

381
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:54,719
How did this happen, my Bey?

382
00:40:56,680 --> 00:40:58,559
The infidels united again.

383
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:01,559
Clearly, it's Sofia's plan. She helped them.

384
00:41:01,600 --> 00:41:06,079
Sofia, Sofia, Sofia. Sofia
is behind everything again.

385
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:11,039
You were right, my Bey. We
did well by evacuating the tribe.

386
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:15,719
But how did you know these
dogs would attack, my Bey?

387
00:41:15,720 --> 00:41:17,599
They have no faith.

388
00:41:17,880 --> 00:41:21,359
I knew they would attack
at our most sacred moment.

389
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:23,199
However...

390
00:41:23,760 --> 00:41:26,199
...their hopes got stuck
in their throats, my Bey.

391
00:41:26,200 --> 00:41:29,239
We will slit that throat soon.

392
00:41:29,240 --> 00:41:32,439
Come on, we are going to
Sogut. This fear is enough for them.

393
00:41:38,480 --> 00:41:44,479
On this blessed night, which is better than
a thousand months, your breath healed us.

394
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:46,119
Thank you.

395
00:41:46,120 --> 00:41:47,359
Don't even mention it.

396
00:41:48,080 --> 00:41:49,799
You hosted us.

397
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:52,799
We were honored to perform our dhikr in Sogut...

398
00:41:52,800 --> 00:41:57,599
...where Sheikh Edebali's
breath touched, Alaeddin Bey.

399
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,919
May Allah be pleased with you.

400
00:42:00,920 --> 00:42:02,119
Thank you.

401
00:42:02,200 --> 00:42:07,199
May Allah grant my Osman Bey and his
descendants many victories, God willing.

402
00:42:08,200 --> 00:42:10,159
Aameen.

403
00:42:11,160 --> 00:42:12,439
Thank you.

404
00:42:12,880 --> 00:42:18,679
May Allah keep your dhikr and breath lasting
in the whole world, God willing, dear Dervish.

405
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:21,879
Thank you. Then we should
ask for your permission to leave.

406
00:42:22,080 --> 00:42:23,239
Don't even ask.

407
00:42:24,120 --> 00:42:26,199
It was a pleasure to meet.

408
00:42:26,680 --> 00:42:28,359
May Allah protect you.

409
00:42:45,760 --> 00:42:46,799
Mother...

410
00:42:48,040 --> 00:42:49,079
Yes my daughter.

411
00:42:51,200 --> 00:42:53,519
I want to ask you something, but...

412
00:42:54,880 --> 00:42:56,359
I am a bit ashamed..

413
00:42:57,280 --> 00:42:58,839
...because I don't know...

414
00:42:58,840 --> 00:43:02,079
Ask me, my daughter. Don't feel
ashamed because you do not know.

415
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:06,519
I've heard it many times from you actually.

416
00:43:07,920 --> 00:43:13,239
I am surprised that I never
wondered about it before.

417
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:19,639
Will you say it, my daughter?

418
00:43:22,520 --> 00:43:27,039
There is no God but Allah.

419
00:43:31,720 --> 00:43:35,719
As if it holds all the
beauty of the world in it.

420
00:43:38,560 --> 00:43:43,879
What is in these words that mesmerizes
Dervishes, you and other Muslims?

421
00:43:44,560 --> 00:43:46,359
Mother, what does it mean?

422
00:43:49,960 --> 00:43:51,649
There is no God (in Arabic)

423
00:43:51,680 --> 00:43:53,679
There is no God (in Turkish)

424
00:43:54,120 --> 00:43:55,319
But Allah (in Arabic)

425
00:43:55,480 --> 00:43:57,519
But Allah (in Turkish)

426
00:43:59,200 --> 00:44:05,479
He is above everything. He is the
Ruler of everything, and the only Creator.

427
00:44:07,360 --> 00:44:09,879
That is the meaning my daughter.

428
00:44:12,520 --> 00:44:15,639
You called it mesmerizing...

429
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:19,639
That word does not mesmerize us.

430
00:44:19,920 --> 00:44:24,359
It is realizing our weakness
before Allah's Greatness.

431
00:44:25,080 --> 00:44:26,199
It is love.

432
00:44:28,400 --> 00:44:30,479
This is what dhikr does to us.

433
00:44:31,600 --> 00:44:34,159
It seems it has touched you too, my daughter.

434
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:38,999
But you will find out
what it means for yourself.

435
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:43,239
Come on.

436
00:44:57,760 --> 00:44:58,959
What happened?

437
00:44:59,680 --> 00:45:01,239
Where have you been, Sargun?

438
00:45:02,160 --> 00:45:06,079
He did not listen to you
and went to attack Osman.

439
00:45:11,360 --> 00:45:12,879
If I had not been there

440
00:45:14,720 --> 00:45:17,079
...they would have fallen into Osman's trap.

441
00:45:19,640 --> 00:45:22,959
A Hanzade does not need your help.

442
00:45:25,880 --> 00:45:30,559
The blood of the Great
Genghis flows in his veins.

443
00:45:30,960 --> 00:45:36,519
If you are from Genghis's lineage, I am
from the lineage of the Great Roman Emperor.

444
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,839
Do not be above yourself.

445
00:45:43,680 --> 00:45:46,399
Those who are above
themselves become Osman's prey.

446
00:45:46,920 --> 00:45:51,959
Just like Commander Ulugan.

447
00:45:54,840 --> 00:45:56,119
Tell me.

448
00:45:57,640 --> 00:45:59,319
Where is he now?

449
00:45:59,800 --> 00:46:00,879
Hatun!

450
00:46:01,760 --> 00:46:03,479
Watch your words.

451
00:46:05,240 --> 00:46:09,959
Or you will become a prisoner of your words!

452
00:46:09,960 --> 00:46:10,999
Soldiers!

453
00:46:18,400 --> 00:46:20,279
Go ahead and kill each other.

454
00:46:22,200 --> 00:46:23,519
Esenbike.

455
00:46:27,640 --> 00:46:31,719
I did not come here to be enemies
I came here to work with you.

456
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:35,159
Because we both have a common enemy.

457
00:46:35,800 --> 00:46:36,839
Osman.

458
00:46:40,880 --> 00:46:41,919
Soldiers!

459
00:46:42,920 --> 00:46:44,279
Get out!

460
00:46:49,280 --> 00:46:51,559
I and Esenbike Hatun...

461
00:46:53,040 --> 00:46:54,919
...have things to talk about.

462
00:46:58,720 --> 00:47:00,319
Everyone leave!

463
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:18,199
So, you went to Osman's tribe to kill him.

464
00:47:19,840 --> 00:47:21,759
Do you have that much power?

465
00:47:25,080 --> 00:47:28,639
To defeat Osman, you need more than just power.

466
00:47:31,560 --> 00:47:33,879
You need wisdom.

467
00:47:37,000 --> 00:47:39,879
Because there is a wolf standing against us.

468
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:44,239
A sneaky and smart wolf.

469
00:47:45,720 --> 00:47:50,079
I turn wolves into fur to wear on my back.

470
00:47:51,320 --> 00:47:54,599
While you were wasting
time in Osman's empty tribe...

471
00:47:55,800 --> 00:47:59,199
...I was planning incredible games here.

472
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:03,239
What kind of a game?

473
00:48:03,800 --> 00:48:06,439
A game that will become a disaster for Osman.

474
00:48:07,720 --> 00:48:13,719
And you will help me against our common enemy.

475
00:48:29,480 --> 00:48:31,039
It was wonderful.

476
00:48:31,160 --> 00:48:34,479
The dhikr of dervishes
purified our hearts, my Osman.

477
00:48:34,640 --> 00:48:36,559
The whole Sogut enjoyed it.

478
00:48:37,160 --> 00:48:39,839
Praise be. Praise be.

479
00:48:40,040 --> 00:48:42,439
But I was thinking about you.

480
00:48:42,680 --> 00:48:44,799
I'm worried about the tribe.

481
00:48:45,120 --> 00:48:49,079
We laid a trap for heathens
but they survived, Bala.

482
00:48:50,920 --> 00:48:54,999
How is the priestess doing? Did she wake up?

483
00:48:55,320 --> 00:48:57,879
We're waiting for the medicine to take effect.

484
00:49:00,720 --> 00:49:05,599
Bala... We'll find our
daughter. You know that, right?

485
00:49:05,680 --> 00:49:07,159
I know.

486
00:49:07,440 --> 00:49:09,279
We'll get our child back.

487
00:49:09,720 --> 00:49:13,159
I know this just like I know
we will take our tribe back.

488
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:15,279
We will take it back.

489
00:49:15,280 --> 00:49:19,879
The reinforcements of the beys are on the
way. I'll welcome them with the alps tomorrow.

490
00:49:20,120 --> 00:49:23,479
We'll take them to the new headquarters.

491
00:49:23,760 --> 00:49:26,919
Praise be. We've lost too many recently.

492
00:49:27,120 --> 00:49:30,199
Our army will get stronger with this.

493
00:49:30,440 --> 00:49:34,239
Yes, don't worry. I'll be cautious all the time.

494
00:49:35,440 --> 00:49:39,519
Gather people with Alaaddin and you
two take them to the new headquarters.

495
00:49:39,520 --> 00:49:42,679
Yes. I'll finish the
preparations quickly, Osman.

496
00:49:42,960 --> 00:49:45,679
We can't stay here any longer, anyway.

497
00:49:45,800 --> 00:49:47,679
No.

498
00:49:49,720 --> 00:49:52,519
No matter what, in case of any hardships

499
00:49:52,760 --> 00:49:55,919
...you stand strong even
without souring your face.

500
00:49:56,280 --> 00:49:59,199
And? Then what?

501
00:49:59,560 --> 00:50:02,599
Well... I fall in love again.

502
00:50:05,560 --> 00:50:07,519
In this world,

503
00:50:08,320 --> 00:50:10,879
...you are my source of gratitude.

504
00:50:11,360 --> 00:50:13,919
You are my source of gratitude, my Osman.

505
00:50:14,520 --> 00:50:16,159
Osman the Brunette.

506
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:19,319
Your eyes are my hopes.

507
00:50:19,960 --> 00:50:22,719
You'll make thing even better than before.

508
00:50:24,120 --> 00:50:25,639
I will.

509
00:50:25,920 --> 00:50:28,079
Don't worry. I will.

510
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:32,279
I will make things right again.

511
00:50:43,680 --> 00:50:46,999
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

512
00:50:49,680 --> 00:50:54,599
The position of the troop to
come is behind that mountain.

513
00:50:58,560 --> 00:51:00,799
We're getting close, but...

514
00:51:01,200 --> 00:51:04,599
...God willing, our alps will arrive
safe and sound too, Osman Bey.

515
00:51:06,360 --> 00:51:09,359
Do you have a problem, Guralp Bey?

516
00:51:12,280 --> 00:51:15,879
Tell us, Guralp Bey. Why are you concerned?

517
00:51:16,080 --> 00:51:17,799
Do you know anything?

518
00:51:18,120 --> 00:51:19,799
I know..

519
00:51:20,080 --> 00:51:23,159
...Esenbike whose tricked got exposed...

520
00:51:23,600 --> 00:51:25,999
...may do any kind of evil things now.

521
00:51:31,400 --> 00:51:33,999
I know why you are concerned.

522
00:51:34,520 --> 00:51:39,119
Esenbike may have realized
that our armies would get united.

523
00:51:42,680 --> 00:51:44,159
But don't worry.

524
00:51:44,560 --> 00:51:47,599
If they use the route we give them

525
00:51:47,960 --> 00:51:51,359
...Mongolians will never notice them.

526
00:51:52,600 --> 00:51:55,679
Come on. Let's go take our warriors.

527
00:52:17,520 --> 00:52:19,159
Alaaddin.

528
00:52:19,160 --> 00:52:22,159
When will this medicine take effect, son?

529
00:52:22,320 --> 00:52:24,119
Shall we give her other medicine?

530
00:52:24,680 --> 00:52:27,959
No, mother. I did everything
that should be done.

531
00:52:28,440 --> 00:52:30,919
We will just wait.

532
00:52:35,680 --> 00:52:38,399
Mother, don't worry.

533
00:52:38,920 --> 00:52:42,519
Obviously, she's a weak one.
That's why it takes effect late.

534
00:52:42,960 --> 00:52:46,599
-She'll open her eyes soon, God willing.
-God willing, Alaaddin Ali.

535
00:52:46,680 --> 00:52:48,439
God willing.

536
00:53:07,800 --> 00:53:11,879
There is a marshland ahead.
Riding the horses may be dangerous.

537
00:53:12,600 --> 00:53:14,519
We'll go on foot.

538
00:53:42,440 --> 00:53:43,799
My Bey.

539
00:53:44,280 --> 00:53:47,959
This silence bothers you too, right?

540
00:53:48,160 --> 00:53:52,599
Even jackals and birds
are making no noise. Well...

541
00:53:53,240 --> 00:53:56,039
You're right.

542
00:53:57,040 --> 00:53:59,479
This place doesn't seem safe.

543
00:54:00,680 --> 00:54:03,279
You're right about your doubts, Osman!

544
00:54:11,200 --> 00:54:13,119
Esenbike.

545
00:54:13,760 --> 00:54:17,319
Wolves, birds and all the
animals have been muted!

546
00:54:17,600 --> 00:54:21,119
Waiting to watch your death!

547
00:54:53,640 --> 00:54:54,959
Osman..

548
00:54:56,360 --> 00:55:00,079
The great commander of Mongolians, Ulugan...

549
00:55:00,240 --> 00:55:04,959
...who you tried to kill and whose
hatred you drew on yourself is here too.

550
00:55:05,560 --> 00:55:07,319
You..

551
00:55:07,920 --> 00:55:09,399
Yes, me.

552
00:55:17,120 --> 00:55:19,599
I will take more from you..

553
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:22,119
...than the pain you left in my chest.

554
00:55:22,120 --> 00:55:26,639
You will regret that I didn't cut you
into a thousand pieces, you vile dog.

555
00:55:28,280 --> 00:55:30,399
We're surrounded, my Bey.

556
00:55:30,720 --> 00:55:32,519
They're too many.

557
00:55:39,680 --> 00:55:44,399
How did they know about our route, my Bey?

558
00:55:45,120 --> 00:55:47,599
It seems their scouts noticed us.

559
00:55:55,440 --> 00:55:57,039
Sahin Bey.

560
00:55:58,800 --> 00:56:02,999
You got my message and came here quickly, huh?

561
00:56:03,680 --> 00:56:05,519
I heard.

562
00:56:06,240 --> 00:56:10,999
You were Osman's guest
for the sake of Qadr night.

563
00:56:11,400 --> 00:56:13,239
Where is my son?

564
00:56:13,760 --> 00:56:15,479
Show him to me now.

565
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:25,599
Your son is alive.

566
00:56:30,560 --> 00:56:32,319
Don't worry.

567
00:56:33,000 --> 00:56:34,839
He's been our guest.

568
00:56:36,280 --> 00:56:38,479
We had some talk.

569
00:56:38,680 --> 00:56:41,599
My son, are you alright?

570
00:56:43,440 --> 00:56:46,599
He's fine. For now.

571
00:56:49,600 --> 00:56:51,399
Don't do this, hatun.

572
00:56:53,400 --> 00:56:56,679
I'll serve you. Don't.

573
00:56:57,680 --> 00:56:59,279
You will.

574
00:57:00,800 --> 00:57:05,319
You will be my servant for your son's life.

575
00:57:13,680 --> 00:57:19,079
You'll tell me about Osman's every step.

576
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:21,559
What now, my Bey?

577
00:57:21,760 --> 00:57:24,119
How will we survive this evil trap?

578
00:57:35,920 --> 00:57:37,439
Kanyumaz.

579
00:57:38,320 --> 00:57:40,679
Take some alps with you.

580
00:57:41,040 --> 00:57:45,679
When we attack, run away before they notice.

581
00:57:46,200 --> 00:57:48,919
Go and meet the Beys.

582
00:57:49,200 --> 00:57:53,159
And take them to Catalkaya.

583
00:57:53,400 --> 00:57:55,119
As you order, my Bey.

584
00:57:57,960 --> 00:58:03,919
Did you become blind and deaf
when you saw our power, Osman?

585
00:58:08,600 --> 00:58:10,679
For the shield wall.

586
00:58:11,360 --> 00:58:13,159
Wait for my call.

587
00:58:13,320 --> 00:58:15,959
-Okay, my Bey.
-What are we waiting for?

588
00:58:16,440 --> 00:58:20,079
-Let's wash our swords with blood!
-Not now, Ulugan!

589
00:58:22,080 --> 00:58:25,199
I want to give Osman a last chance.

590
00:58:25,640 --> 00:58:27,879
What is it?

591
00:58:28,200 --> 00:58:29,599
Let me know!

592
00:58:29,800 --> 00:58:32,079
A chance to live, Osman.

593
00:58:32,560 --> 00:58:33,879
You'll see.

594
00:58:34,160 --> 00:58:38,119
Before you could reach the armies
you were expecting, you got trapped!

595
00:58:38,600 --> 00:58:40,839
Now drop your sword and surrender.

596
00:58:44,760 --> 00:58:46,759
...won't lose their lives.

597
00:58:47,280 --> 00:58:49,039
Fools, huh?

598
00:58:49,640 --> 00:58:52,159
The ones behind me are Turks!

599
00:58:53,520 --> 00:58:56,999
Don't confuse them with your looters!

600
00:58:58,400 --> 00:59:01,239
A wolf never walks not to die.

601
00:59:01,920 --> 00:59:05,559
You may be stronger than us.

602
00:59:06,080 --> 00:59:09,439
But you can never...

603
00:59:09,880 --> 00:59:13,799
...wipe us out of people's hearts!

604
00:59:14,640 --> 00:59:16,559
We may fall on the ground!

605
00:59:17,120 --> 00:59:21,599
But our names, reputations
and our children following us...

606
00:59:21,800 --> 00:59:26,319
...will always make people like you pay for it!

607
00:59:31,880 --> 00:59:34,639
-Close.
-Alps, shield wall!

608
00:59:35,680 --> 00:59:37,679
Archers, attack!

609
00:59:37,720 --> 00:59:39,999
Nokers, shield wall!

610
00:59:41,120 --> 00:59:44,839
Shield wall, nokers!

611
00:59:45,040 --> 00:59:46,319
Open!

612
00:59:47,440 --> 00:59:48,959
Close!

613
00:59:49,120 --> 00:59:50,839
Kanyumaz.
-My Bey.

614
00:59:51,000 --> 00:59:53,799
-Go now. As you order, my Bey.

615
00:59:56,440 --> 00:59:58,359
Open!

616
00:59:59,560 --> 01:00:02,079
-Close!
-Open!

617
01:00:12,920 --> 01:00:15,919
Open! Close!

618
01:00:41,160 --> 01:00:44,439
Close! Open!

619
01:00:52,120 --> 01:00:55,439
My Bey, arrows are raining over us.

620
01:01:02,360 --> 01:01:04,799
Ambush! Alaaddin!

621
01:01:05,000 --> 01:01:06,799
Alps, take position!

622
01:01:06,840 --> 01:01:10,799
-Bala!
-Ulgen, take women and children into the woods.

623
01:01:17,160 --> 01:01:20,319
You snake. You never die!

624
01:01:24,920 --> 01:01:26,639
Bala!

625
01:01:27,320 --> 01:01:28,959
This is the end.

626
01:01:30,280 --> 01:01:32,359
Kill them all!

627
01:01:32,640 --> 01:01:34,799
Attack!

628
01:01:46,240 --> 01:01:49,199
It's time for the unfinished business, Bala.

629
01:02:00,520 --> 01:02:02,119
I'll be your death, Begum.

630
01:03:09,080 --> 01:03:11,519
Hide. Protect yourself.

631
01:03:14,240 --> 01:03:17,999
If the priestess wakes up, she'll try
to harm you to take revenge from me.

632
01:03:18,200 --> 01:03:19,679
Hide.

633
01:03:26,400 --> 01:03:28,759
Protect the priestess!

634
01:03:36,560 --> 01:03:38,919
You'll never be able to reach your target.

635
01:03:39,040 --> 01:03:41,119
I have to kill you first then, huh?

636
01:03:47,240 --> 01:03:51,039
That's not going to happen, Sofia.
Today, you are the ones to die!

637
01:04:00,600 --> 01:04:02,559
Attack!

638
01:04:13,160 --> 01:04:14,879
Close!

639
01:04:17,200 --> 01:04:18,799
Open!

640
01:04:21,440 --> 01:04:22,719
Close!

641
01:04:23,760 --> 01:04:25,479
Open!

642
01:04:29,880 --> 01:04:31,919
Hold on, warrior. Hold on.

643
01:04:33,440 --> 01:04:34,919
Come on.

644
01:04:36,080 --> 01:04:38,839
-Orhan, your turn.
-Alright.

645
01:04:39,280 --> 01:04:42,359
Their resistance got broken,
Esenbike. We should attack.

646
01:04:42,480 --> 01:04:46,079
There is still time. Keep shooting arrows!

647
01:04:51,880 --> 01:04:54,399
Do they never run out of arrows?

648
01:04:54,600 --> 01:04:57,679
When they do, you'll see what I'm going to do.

649
01:04:57,920 --> 01:04:59,759
We're trapped here.

650
01:04:59,920 --> 01:05:02,359
Are these shields enough to protect us?

651
01:05:02,520 --> 01:05:06,759
My Bey, if we don't attack now
we may never get out of here.

652
01:05:06,760 --> 01:05:08,799
No, just wait.

653
01:05:09,200 --> 01:05:12,399
We have to hold on. Be patient.

654
01:05:14,120 --> 01:05:16,759
I'm out of patience. Attack, nokers!

655
01:05:18,840 --> 01:05:20,599
They're attacking, my Bey.

656
01:05:20,600 --> 01:05:23,159
-We should leave the cover.
-We'll wait, Cerkutay.

657
01:05:23,160 --> 01:05:25,079
We have to wait.

658
01:05:26,640 --> 01:05:28,599
Draw your swords.

659
01:05:30,640 --> 01:05:32,759
Open!

660
01:05:35,960 --> 01:05:37,799
Open!

661
01:05:41,600 --> 01:05:43,079
Osman...

662
01:05:43,440 --> 01:05:45,839
...isn't going to give up, Esenbike Hatun.

663
01:05:50,360 --> 01:05:52,079
Open!

664
01:05:57,160 --> 01:05:58,479
My Bey!

665
01:05:58,600 --> 01:05:59,879
-My Bey!
-My Bey!

666
01:05:59,920 --> 01:06:01,359
Are you alright, my Bey?

667
01:06:02,520 --> 01:06:04,519
I'm fine, don't worry.

668
01:06:06,600 --> 01:06:08,359
It's just a tiny wound!

669
01:06:08,680 --> 01:06:11,999
You'll face the cold side of my sword shortly!

670
01:06:12,240 --> 01:06:14,959
Your daring will bring your death, Ulugan!

671
01:06:15,480 --> 01:06:17,599
Time is ticking for you!

672
01:06:19,320 --> 01:06:21,639
Time is ticking for you.

673
01:07:53,920 --> 01:07:56,239
Come on, warriors!

674
01:08:20,479 --> 01:08:22,118
Your end has come, Begum

675
01:08:23,680 --> 01:08:26,919
-I will not die before I kill you, Bala!
-Say the shahada!

676
01:08:36,640 --> 01:08:37,719
Traitor!

677
01:09:00,680 --> 01:09:01,439
Gonca.

678
01:09:02,040 --> 01:09:05,759
You go to the cart, protect the
Priestess. We will handle this here.

679
01:09:05,760 --> 01:09:08,038
How can I leave you alone, Holofira?

680
01:09:15,880 --> 01:09:17,879
Gonca, come on, they are coming.

681
01:10:14,920 --> 01:10:17,879
There are too many of them,
Holofira. Come on, let's go.

682
01:10:17,880 --> 01:10:22,359
Ulgen, gather the people.

683
01:10:27,240 --> 01:10:30,919
Mother. Mother, they are killing
the people, what will we do now?

684
01:10:32,360 --> 01:10:35,359
We are retreating. To the
horses, to the cart, come on.

685
01:10:36,640 --> 01:10:39,119
Do you think we will let you go, Alaeddin?

686
01:10:40,280 --> 01:10:42,519
We will see. We will see.

687
01:10:42,520 --> 01:10:43,759
Come on, to the horses.

688
01:10:43,760 --> 01:10:45,639
They are escaping. Run.

689
01:10:46,120 --> 01:10:47,959
Run!

690
01:10:47,960 --> 01:10:50,519
Alps! Flying flames!

691
01:11:07,320 --> 01:11:08,679
They escaped!

692
01:11:11,880 --> 01:11:12,919
Bala!

693
01:11:20,320 --> 01:11:22,839
Do not stop! Kill them with your swords!

694
01:11:22,840 --> 01:11:25,039
Now!

695
01:11:29,760 --> 01:11:31,719
My Bey, their nokers are too many.

696
01:11:31,960 --> 01:11:35,239
We cannot fight them with a few men.

697
01:11:35,240 --> 01:11:37,679
We had them place the nokers across the region.

698
01:11:37,800 --> 01:11:40,199
Now we will lure them to us.

699
01:11:40,200 --> 01:11:41,279
Come on, Alps!

700
01:11:43,600 --> 01:11:45,159
Now!

701
01:11:58,880 --> 01:12:00,799
You are running Osman, huh?

702
01:12:02,360 --> 01:12:04,159
Now they will come after me.

703
01:12:04,160 --> 01:12:06,479
Boran and I will go north.

704
01:12:06,480 --> 01:12:09,279
Orhan, you will go south.

705
01:12:09,360 --> 01:12:10,679
They will follow us.

706
01:12:10,680 --> 01:12:15,639
After we get rid of them, you
will go to Catalkaya with the Beys.

707
01:12:15,640 --> 01:12:19,279
Ulugan! Go after him! Catch Osman!

708
01:12:22,120 --> 01:12:25,159
-Come on, to the horses.
-Come on, Beys.

709
01:12:25,160 --> 01:12:27,959
Sargun, you go after Ulugan as well.

710
01:12:28,320 --> 01:12:31,439
As you order, mother.

711
01:12:38,680 --> 01:12:42,319
Alaeddin, how is the Priestess?
Did you check her, my son?

712
01:12:42,320 --> 01:12:44,399
I did, mother. She is alright.

713
01:12:44,400 --> 01:12:45,399
Good.

714
01:12:46,000 --> 01:12:49,519
The fog has slowed them
down a lot. They cannot catch us.

715
01:12:49,520 --> 01:12:53,359
We will continue through this
forest. They will not find us this way.

716
01:12:53,360 --> 01:12:55,039
This way! Come on! -Come on!

717
01:13:17,040 --> 01:13:18,999
My Bey, are you alright?

718
01:13:19,000 --> 01:13:20,439
I am alright. I am.

719
01:13:20,480 --> 01:13:23,719
My Bey, your wound has weakened
you. We need to cauterize it.

720
01:13:24,920 --> 01:13:28,159
Esenbike revealed our plan.

721
01:13:28,560 --> 01:13:30,999
Let's first get rid of those following us.

722
01:13:31,120 --> 01:13:34,599
Then we need to determine
the route with the Beys.

723
01:13:35,480 --> 01:13:37,799
My Bey, there is a cave ahead.

724
01:13:37,800 --> 01:13:41,079
At least we can stop the
bleeding there. Then we can go.

725
01:13:41,080 --> 01:13:42,359
Come on my Bey...

726
01:13:42,680 --> 01:13:44,439
Let's hide the horses then.

727
01:14:02,800 --> 01:14:06,239
Altuga... Find where they are.

728
01:14:21,120 --> 01:14:22,679
Hurry, Altuga.

729
01:14:28,040 --> 01:14:30,599
They cannot have gone too far with that wound.

730
01:14:31,480 --> 01:14:33,719
They are somewhere around here.

731
01:14:36,840 --> 01:14:38,359
Where are they, Altuga?

732
01:14:39,840 --> 01:14:41,479
They went this way, Ulugan.

733
01:14:56,520 --> 01:14:59,269
Osman Bey Headquarters

734
01:15:13,360 --> 01:15:16,439
Alps, take the wounded to
the healing tents, come on.

735
01:15:17,800 --> 01:15:20,839
Gonca, take the Priestess
to the tent, my daughter.

736
01:15:21,080 --> 01:15:21,999
As you order, mother.

737
01:15:22,000 --> 01:15:26,799
Alps, send out watchmen immediately.
Take positions around the quarters.

738
01:15:26,840 --> 01:15:30,679
I do not want any weakness know that. Come on.

739
01:15:39,080 --> 01:15:40,119
Slowly...

740
01:15:47,920 --> 01:15:51,559
Those dogs will not hold
back. Sofia is after the Priestess.

741
01:15:51,560 --> 01:15:54,439
Kismet, place the sisters
at the Priestess' door.

742
01:15:57,840 --> 01:15:58,879
Bala Hatun.

743
01:15:59,440 --> 01:16:03,919
That woman, Sofia... Why did
she want to kill the Priestess?

744
01:16:03,920 --> 01:16:04,999
Isn't she her friend?

745
01:16:05,000 --> 01:16:08,159
She is cruel enough to kill the woman
who has been her companion for years.

746
01:16:08,160 --> 01:16:11,027
She does not love anyone. She
doesn't know what friendship is.

747
01:16:11,039 --> 01:16:11,999
Mother...

748
01:16:12,960 --> 01:16:14,479
You know, they attacked us...

749
01:16:15,120 --> 01:16:17,839
What if they attack my father and Orhan?

750
01:16:17,840 --> 01:16:19,439
May Allah forbid, my daughter.

751
01:16:20,320 --> 01:16:23,399
God willing they are safe.
Nothing bad will happen.

752
01:16:24,480 --> 01:16:27,279
You look a little pale. Take some rest.

753
01:16:27,280 --> 01:16:30,679
Fatma, your aunt is entrusted to you.
-Do not worry, mother.

754
01:16:30,720 --> 01:16:31,759
Come on.

755
01:16:31,960 --> 01:16:33,399
Mother.

756
01:16:34,960 --> 01:16:36,839
Lucia is not well.

757
01:16:37,160 --> 01:16:39,239
She moved too much her wound opened.

758
01:16:39,240 --> 01:16:41,959
Alaeddin, do your best
and help her survive, my son.

759
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:43,799
She will bring Halime to us.

760
01:16:43,800 --> 01:16:46,559
If necessary, I will wait
next to her until she dies.

761
01:16:47,320 --> 01:16:48,919
I will do my best, mother.

762
01:16:48,920 --> 01:16:50,639
I need to talk to Lucia.

763
01:16:50,640 --> 01:16:52,439
Come on, son, come on.

764
01:16:53,520 --> 01:16:54,559
Come on.

765
01:16:54,760 --> 01:16:55,839
Bala Hatun.

766
01:16:56,000 --> 01:16:59,239
I can stay with Lucia. If she
wakes up, I will let you know.

767
01:16:59,280 --> 01:17:00,559
You have a lot to do.

768
01:17:01,480 --> 01:17:03,959
That would be very good, my daughter. Very good.

769
01:17:03,960 --> 01:17:07,199
Then I entrust my daughter
and her secret to you, alright?

770
01:17:07,680 --> 01:17:10,919
I promise. I will not even blink there.

771
01:17:11,440 --> 01:17:15,039
Good.

772
01:17:32,120 --> 01:17:33,719
Rider nokers...

773
01:17:34,120 --> 01:17:38,079
Those dastards are replaced
by new ones the moment they die.

774
01:17:39,600 --> 01:17:40,919
Let them come.

775
01:17:41,560 --> 01:17:44,119
We will keep fighting until we kill them all.

776
01:17:49,320 --> 01:17:50,359
Come on!

777
01:18:29,760 --> 01:18:30,799
That's all!

778
01:18:31,120 --> 01:18:32,479
No one else is coming.

779
01:18:33,440 --> 01:18:36,839
Ulugan sent most of his nokers after Osman Bey.

780
01:18:37,240 --> 01:18:38,919
God willing my Bey is alright.

781
01:18:40,120 --> 01:18:41,439
With that wound...

782
01:18:41,680 --> 01:18:44,199
...it will be difficult for him to escape.

783
01:18:45,120 --> 01:18:48,079
Are we going to ask for a
support unit for Osman Bey?

784
01:18:54,240 --> 01:18:55,279
No...

785
01:18:56,400 --> 01:18:58,759
We will follow Osman Bey's orders.

786
01:19:00,120 --> 01:19:01,199
Get ready.

787
01:19:01,520 --> 01:19:03,519
We will wait for him at Catalkaya.

788
01:19:24,440 --> 01:19:26,359
I cannot understand, my Bey...

789
01:19:27,440 --> 01:19:29,119
I keep thinking...

790
01:19:29,200 --> 01:19:30,959
But I cannot find its answer.

791
01:19:32,840 --> 01:19:33,999
Esenbike..

792
01:19:34,160 --> 01:19:36,679
How did she find out about our route?

793
01:19:37,280 --> 01:19:38,319
Clearly...

794
01:19:38,680 --> 01:19:40,919
Clearly, there is a traitor among us.

795
01:19:41,880 --> 01:19:44,039
Who do you think it is, my Bey? Which dog?

796
01:19:45,320 --> 01:19:47,719
He will show up in the end...

797
01:19:47,880 --> 01:19:50,399
We will punish him when he shows up.

798
01:19:51,680 --> 01:19:53,679
But now, what matter is to...

799
01:19:54,120 --> 01:19:59,999
...get over this hardship as soon as
possible before we lose more men.

800
01:20:01,160 --> 01:20:03,799
My Bey, Ulugan and his dogs are after us.

801
01:20:03,800 --> 01:20:05,839
They are looking for you everywhere.

802
01:20:05,880 --> 01:20:07,319
We will get out, but how?

803
01:20:07,720 --> 01:20:10,119
That's better... Let him come after us.

804
01:20:10,480 --> 01:20:13,759
While he is after us, we'll change our plan...

805
01:20:14,280 --> 01:20:15,839
...and go to the tribe.

806
01:20:17,160 --> 01:20:20,279
My Bey, we have not gathered our army yet.

807
01:20:20,320 --> 01:20:22,599
Alright, we cauterized your wound.

808
01:20:22,600 --> 01:20:25,199
But this wound will weaken you, my Bey.

809
01:20:25,760 --> 01:20:28,919
How are we going to take the
tribe when we are in this state?

810
01:20:28,920 --> 01:20:31,439
I will explain how when we meet with the Beys.

811
01:20:31,800 --> 01:20:33,559
Now go to Bala..

812
01:20:33,760 --> 01:20:35,839
Tell her what happened.

813
01:20:35,840 --> 01:20:39,479
They will go to the tribe from the quarters.

814
01:20:41,520 --> 01:20:43,759
As you order my Bey.

815
01:21:07,280 --> 01:21:10,959
This cave is the only place we
haven't checked around here, Ulugan.

816
01:21:48,960 --> 01:21:50,039
They are here.

817
01:21:50,040 --> 01:21:51,119
Spread out!

818
01:21:51,120 --> 01:21:52,279
Check everywhere!

819
01:21:53,240 --> 01:21:54,839
They found us, my Bey.

820
01:22:19,680 --> 01:22:22,039
Why did my aunt want to kill you?

821
01:22:24,280 --> 01:22:26,799
Why did you say Halime's name was Poena?

822
01:22:29,520 --> 01:22:30,559
Please, wake up.

823
01:22:31,800 --> 01:22:32,839
Lucia..

824
01:22:41,680 --> 01:22:43,479
Poena, is that you?

825
01:22:43,960 --> 01:22:45,679
Thank God, you are alive.

826
01:22:48,600 --> 01:22:50,719
Why did my aunt do this?

827
01:22:51,560 --> 01:22:52,879
She loves you.

828
01:22:53,800 --> 01:22:56,599
She cannot love anyone. Poena.

829
01:23:00,280 --> 01:23:01,359
Are you alright?

830
01:23:03,680 --> 01:23:05,119
I am confused.

831
01:23:07,040 --> 01:23:08,719
My aunt said Halime was dead.

832
01:23:11,000 --> 01:23:13,919
Why did you tell Bala my name?

833
01:23:15,320 --> 01:23:16,679
Sofia.

834
01:23:17,520 --> 01:23:18,839
Sofia.

835
01:23:22,080 --> 01:23:23,479
Don't trust her.

836
01:23:25,000 --> 01:23:28,879
You cannot trust her.

837
01:23:30,520 --> 01:23:31,559
Bala.

838
01:23:32,960 --> 01:23:34,159
Bala.

839
01:23:34,880 --> 01:23:36,319
What do you mean?

840
01:23:37,120 --> 01:23:38,159
My aunt means.

841
01:23:38,840 --> 01:23:40,039
...the world to me.

842
01:23:42,000 --> 01:23:43,519
She is my only family.

843
01:23:44,480 --> 01:23:45,519
Did you forget?

844
01:23:46,640 --> 01:23:47,679
Bala killed..

845
01:23:48,320 --> 01:23:49,559
...my mother!

846
01:23:51,840 --> 01:23:54,039
May God forgive us.

847
01:23:55,080 --> 01:23:56,759
Forgive me Poena.

848
01:23:58,960 --> 01:24:01,399
Tell me Lucia.

849
01:24:01,400 --> 01:24:02,759
Halime died, right?

850
01:24:03,880 --> 01:24:05,439
My aunt is telling the truth...

851
01:24:08,200 --> 01:24:09,319
Halime...

852
01:24:11,800 --> 01:24:13,799
Halime is alive.

853
01:24:20,760 --> 01:24:21,999
Now Osman...

854
01:24:22,560 --> 01:24:24,559
...then Orhan will die.

855
01:24:25,120 --> 01:24:28,359
As long as our spy Sahin is among them...

856
01:24:29,280 --> 01:24:32,039
...every step they will take will be useless.

857
01:24:59,360 --> 01:25:00,639
Osman..

858
01:25:02,840 --> 01:25:06,639
You were afraid of becoming my
prey and took refuge in this cave, huh?

859
01:25:06,840 --> 01:25:08,079
Right...

860
01:25:08,680 --> 01:25:11,199
When jackals invade the wolf's tent...

861
01:25:12,040 --> 01:25:15,679
...the wolf will surely revive in a cave.

862
01:25:20,760 --> 01:25:23,519
I also wanted to finish what we started.

863
01:25:24,480 --> 01:25:25,919
Now it is time.

864
01:25:26,160 --> 01:25:26,959
Now...

865
01:25:27,400 --> 01:25:30,199
You should forget about resurrection.

866
01:25:30,320 --> 01:25:32,119
These are your final moments.

867
01:25:32,800 --> 01:25:34,119
Is that so?

868
01:25:38,920 --> 01:25:40,719
We'll see now.

869
01:25:43,920 --> 01:25:45,159
Flying flame!

870
01:25:45,320 --> 01:25:46,359
Come on!

871
01:26:13,920 --> 01:26:16,559
My Bey.. Are you alright?
-I am.

872
01:26:18,240 --> 01:26:22,239
My Bey, God willing we can
find a way out as you said.

873
01:26:22,240 --> 01:26:23,559
We will.

874
01:26:26,560 --> 01:26:28,679
There is a light over there.

875
01:26:29,080 --> 01:26:30,999
I guess there's a way, let's go.

876
01:26:31,000 --> 01:26:32,199
Okay my Bey..

877
01:26:57,800 --> 01:26:59,719
Has Osman lost his mind?

878
01:27:00,240 --> 01:27:04,159
He trapped himself inside to escape from us.

879
01:27:04,320 --> 01:27:06,959
So just to turn this cave into our grave...

880
01:27:07,200 --> 01:27:09,679
...you gave up on yourself too, Osman.

881
01:27:10,160 --> 01:27:15,199
Osman wouldn't do this if
he hadn't planned a way out.

882
01:27:15,840 --> 01:27:17,839
We will look for another way.

883
01:27:17,960 --> 01:27:19,799
Come on. Start walking around.

884
01:27:19,880 --> 01:27:20,919
Come on.

885
01:27:49,800 --> 01:27:53,119
He won't expect us to get out from this place.

886
01:27:53,120 --> 01:27:54,719
They must be after us.

887
01:27:54,720 --> 01:27:55,999
Let's go to the horses.

888
01:27:56,920 --> 01:27:59,679
And you will go to the quarters immediately.

889
01:27:59,680 --> 01:28:01,319
Inform Bala Hatun.

890
01:28:01,360 --> 01:28:02,719
Now they will set out...

891
01:28:02,880 --> 01:28:06,119
...to the tribe from the quarters.

892
01:28:06,440 --> 01:28:09,559
My Bey, as you order, but...

893
01:28:10,520 --> 01:28:11,559
But what?

894
01:28:12,960 --> 01:28:15,239
My Bey, your wound seems really deep.

895
01:28:15,320 --> 01:28:17,079
I cannot leave you alone here.

896
01:28:17,080 --> 01:28:18,759
Do not make me repeat my word!

897
01:28:18,800 --> 01:28:24,559
If we need to die, we will die! Today,
our banner will be raised in our tribe!

898
01:28:25,520 --> 01:28:26,559
As you order my Bey.

899
01:28:26,680 --> 01:28:30,359
Hurry up! Look under every
stone! Check everywhere!

900
01:28:31,640 --> 01:28:34,719
They are coming. Come on, to the horses!

901
01:28:35,800 --> 01:28:37,359
Let's go!

902
01:28:59,960 --> 01:29:01,359
They got out from here.

903
01:29:06,160 --> 01:29:07,879
We'll go after them now.

904
01:29:09,600 --> 01:29:11,439
Not we, Ulugan.

905
01:29:12,080 --> 01:29:15,319
Altuga will.

906
01:29:15,320 --> 01:29:17,639
You and I will go to my mother.

907
01:29:20,440 --> 01:29:22,519
Apparently, this Osman won't stop.

908
01:29:23,400 --> 01:29:26,319
We will ask her what to do.

909
01:29:38,920 --> 01:29:43,359
So you are saying these are all the
Turkmen Beys that have come to Catalkaya.

910
01:29:43,960 --> 01:29:45,359
Is that right, Kanyumaz?

911
01:29:45,360 --> 01:29:48,439
There are this many people on their way as
well who have received our word my Shahzade.

912
01:29:48,440 --> 01:29:50,999
With Allah's permission they will arrive soon.

913
01:29:51,320 --> 01:29:52,359
Alright.

914
01:29:58,600 --> 01:30:01,319
My Shahzade, Osman Bey is coming.

915
01:30:09,240 --> 01:30:11,079
Clear the way.

916
01:30:15,640 --> 01:30:17,079
Come here, you traitor...

917
01:30:17,680 --> 01:30:18,999
Come here..

918
01:30:19,760 --> 01:30:21,599
Show yourself!

919
01:30:23,640 --> 01:30:25,639
Who are you talking to, Osman Bey?

920
01:30:31,240 --> 01:30:33,439
The traitor among us knows who he is.

921
01:30:33,920 --> 01:30:35,239
Show yourself!

922
01:31:01,840 --> 01:31:02,879
My Bey..

923
01:31:03,520 --> 01:31:04,599
Forgive me.

924
01:31:08,360 --> 01:31:10,039
Forgiveness, huh?

925
01:31:10,720 --> 01:31:12,959
Then... Kneel

926
01:31:13,000 --> 01:31:15,159
How can you ask for forgiveness?

927
01:31:25,960 --> 01:31:27,239
Forgive me, my Bey!

928
01:31:37,320 --> 01:31:38,279
So

929
01:31:39,680 --> 01:31:43,559
...you were the one who informed
Esenbike of our route, huh?

930
01:31:44,120 --> 01:31:46,319
So you lured us into a trap.

931
01:31:47,480 --> 01:31:51,199
So you were the reason of all
the lives we've lost, is that right?

932
01:31:54,240 --> 01:31:55,279
Huh?

933
01:31:56,160 --> 01:32:00,639
My Bey, how did you find that out?

934
01:32:12,760 --> 01:32:15,279
How did I learn about this?

935
01:32:28,360 --> 01:32:32,439
First Osman and then Orhan are going to die.

936
01:32:32,680 --> 01:32:35,759
As long as our spy Sahin is among them

937
01:32:35,960 --> 01:32:38,479
...we'll know about their every step.

938
01:32:44,920 --> 01:32:47,519
They threatened me with my son's life, my Bey.

939
01:32:47,800 --> 01:32:50,679
I made a mistake. Please.

940
01:32:51,240 --> 01:32:53,679
Forgive me.
-Shut up!

941
01:32:56,520 --> 01:32:58,159
Shut up!

942
01:33:00,760 --> 01:33:02,559
I will never forgive you.

943
01:33:03,440 --> 01:33:09,239
For your own son's life,

944
01:33:10,960 --> 01:33:14,519
...you sacrificed many sons of the state, huh?

945
01:33:14,800 --> 01:33:17,679
Huh? For yourself!

946
01:33:18,160 --> 01:33:23,319
You sacrificed all those Beys
and alps who would die for freedom!

947
01:33:27,440 --> 01:33:29,919
Look at me! Look!

948
01:33:30,200 --> 01:33:31,559
No.

949
01:33:31,880 --> 01:33:37,719
Even if I forgive you as a father,

950
01:33:45,200 --> 01:33:51,319
...the state will never forgive this betrayal.

951
01:34:06,920 --> 01:34:12,319
He's neither the first nor
the last traitor among us!

952
01:34:14,120 --> 01:34:20,209
But traitors like him can never stop
the ones walking in the right path!

953
01:34:20,209 --> 01:34:21,479
Definitely, my Bey.

954
01:34:21,600 --> 01:34:24,319
This vile dog ruined the plan...

955
01:34:24,600 --> 01:34:28,319
...that we created with great efforts.

956
01:34:29,640 --> 01:34:32,239
Some more reinforcements units are on the way.

957
01:34:32,520 --> 01:34:37,359
Mongolians know our intention now. How
can we gather them in the headquarters?

958
01:34:38,960 --> 01:34:40,159
No.

959
01:34:40,720 --> 01:34:42,959
We aren't going to the headquarters.

960
01:34:44,680 --> 01:34:47,079
We're going somewhere else.

961
01:34:53,040 --> 01:34:57,199
How could Bala run away with a
few Turkmen from all those nokers?

962
01:34:57,400 --> 01:35:00,599
We lost their traces after the dense forest.

963
01:35:01,520 --> 01:35:04,159
Yet we will definitely catch them, Esenbike.

964
01:35:07,200 --> 01:35:12,039
If you let them win again, I
will choke you myself, Ilbay.

965
01:35:16,400 --> 01:35:19,199
Osman has run away, Esenbike.

966
01:35:21,120 --> 01:35:23,359
Nokers are tracing them.

967
01:35:25,200 --> 01:35:27,079
What now?

968
01:35:27,560 --> 01:35:31,159
If you leave the prey
wounded, he will be the predator.

969
01:35:31,880 --> 01:35:34,559
Osman will continue his plan.

970
01:35:35,120 --> 01:35:38,599
We'll kill him before he gathers the units.

971
01:35:43,160 --> 01:35:49,039
Ilbay, go to the tribe quickly and
take measures in case of a riot.

972
01:35:52,080 --> 01:35:59,639
We'll take out Osman's and his men's
hearts and make Mongolians prevail!

973
01:36:05,680 --> 01:36:07,359
All those alps hit the road.

974
01:36:07,360 --> 01:36:11,119
...crossed the border and reached
Kayi lands dealing with troubles.

975
01:36:11,280 --> 01:36:14,559
But now you say the plan has changed, Osman Bey.

976
01:36:15,080 --> 01:36:16,839
What's in your mind, Osman Bey?

977
01:36:16,920 --> 01:36:19,719
Will we send our men back to our tribes?

978
01:36:20,320 --> 01:36:22,999
The way back must be full of ambushes and traps.

979
01:36:23,440 --> 01:36:27,319
That way will lead our men to death.

980
01:36:28,000 --> 01:36:30,599
I said we won't go to the headquarters.

981
01:36:31,120 --> 01:36:34,079
But I didn't say we will give up.

982
01:36:35,360 --> 01:36:39,639
Our enemies will think we're going to
gather our armies in the headquarters.

983
01:36:39,720 --> 01:36:42,239
They'll think we intend to do that.

984
01:36:42,640 --> 01:36:44,439
Let them think so.

985
01:36:44,720 --> 01:36:47,279
They will be looking for us everywhere.

986
01:36:47,520 --> 01:36:53,119
But we will march towards Kayi
Tribe that they left unprotected.

987
01:36:55,920 --> 01:36:57,359
Remember!

988
01:36:57,480 --> 01:36:59,839
We have a tribe to save from the dark clouds...

989
01:36:59,920 --> 01:37:05,079
..and a cause with whose light
will spread all around the world!

990
01:37:06,080 --> 01:37:09,039
We have swords to pierce
the chests of our enemies...

991
01:37:09,440 --> 01:37:13,039
...and a revenge to take for the
sake of the oppressed people!

992
01:37:17,280 --> 01:37:21,399
For Allah! For the state!

993
01:37:23,760 --> 01:37:28,679
For the future of Turks,
we have a long way to go!

994
01:37:28,800 --> 01:37:32,039
-Your way is our way, Osman Bey!
-Thank you!

995
01:37:32,360 --> 01:37:45,389
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

996
01:37:46,720 --> 01:37:48,599
Where is Halime?

997
01:37:48,840 --> 01:37:51,319
Tell me where my daughter is.

998
01:37:51,960 --> 01:37:53,959
Tell me where she is.

999
01:37:58,240 --> 01:38:01,959
She's with Sofia.

1000
01:38:09,400 --> 01:38:11,959
Don't sleep. Lucia, don't sleep.

1001
01:38:12,120 --> 01:38:15,359
Look at me. Don't go! Look at me.

1002
01:38:16,000 --> 01:38:17,799
Poena.

1003
01:38:18,920 --> 01:38:20,159
Halime.

1004
01:38:20,320 --> 01:38:21,719
She's my Halime.

1005
01:38:21,800 --> 01:38:23,559
Doesn't she remember?

1006
01:38:23,920 --> 01:38:26,079
What did that snake do to my daughter?

1007
01:38:26,120 --> 01:38:28,039
She doesn't remember.

1008
01:38:28,680 --> 01:38:30,199
Sofia..

1009
01:38:30,480 --> 01:38:34,839
She's much worse than you think.

1010
01:38:36,680 --> 01:38:39,439
Tell me. How can I recognize her?

1011
01:38:39,880 --> 01:38:42,319
Where is Halime? Tell me.

1012
01:38:42,640 --> 01:38:44,439
How can I find her?

1013
01:38:49,600 --> 01:38:51,519
Very...

1014
01:38:53,960 --> 01:38:56,239
..close.

1015
01:39:00,880 --> 01:39:03,799
Mother! Mother!

1016
01:39:05,320 --> 01:39:08,439
-Son.
-Mother, a message from father.

1017
01:39:08,600 --> 01:39:11,199
What is it? What's going on, Boran?

1018
01:39:11,200 --> 01:39:13,719
My Bey says we'll take
our tribe back, Bala Hatun.

1019
01:39:13,960 --> 01:39:17,639
He'll wait near the tribe
for us, alps and sisters.

1020
01:39:18,160 --> 01:39:21,319
-Thanks to Allah. Today is the day, huh?
-Yes.

1021
01:39:22,440 --> 01:39:26,999
Fine. You gather alps and
sisters. We need to go. Come on.

1022
01:39:27,240 --> 01:39:28,599
As you order, mother.

1023
01:39:28,760 --> 01:39:31,199
-Let's go, Boran Bey.
-Okay.

1024
01:39:31,600 --> 01:39:33,999
My girl, look after her.

1025
01:39:51,400 --> 01:39:54,959
Watch around carefully! Stand
on alert until we find Osman!

1026
01:39:55,200 --> 01:39:57,439
Come on, come on!

1027
01:40:09,560 --> 01:40:13,399
Stand on alert until we find
Osman! Come on, come on!

1028
01:40:42,800 --> 01:40:44,679
Everything is for you.

1029
01:40:46,360 --> 01:40:47,839
Everything.

1030
01:41:12,440 --> 01:41:14,439
I wasn't born as a Kayi.

1031
01:41:16,600 --> 01:41:18,759
I became a Kayi.

1032
01:41:25,400 --> 01:41:28,959
I killed Ilbay for the chair.

1033
01:41:32,280 --> 01:41:34,039
I became Ilbay.

1034
01:41:41,000 --> 01:41:43,359
While I still had his blood on my hands,

1035
01:41:45,680 --> 01:41:47,839
...I became a father for her daughter.

1036
01:41:53,360 --> 01:41:55,919
I became the devil's servant for this chair.

1037
01:41:59,680 --> 01:42:02,119
Nobody can take this chair from me.

1038
01:42:03,000 --> 01:42:04,959
Nobody.

1039
01:42:08,360 --> 01:42:12,879
Osman has surrounded the
tribe. They're coming. Too many.

1040
01:42:13,480 --> 01:42:16,639
Never!

1041
01:42:16,800 --> 01:42:18,319
We won't let them!

1042
01:42:18,920 --> 01:42:20,479
Come on!

1043
01:42:47,800 --> 01:42:49,239
You..

1044
01:42:50,200 --> 01:42:52,119
...aren't my father.

1045
01:42:52,480 --> 01:42:55,879
You are a lying murderer.

1046
01:43:06,920 --> 01:43:08,399
My Bey.

1047
01:43:09,480 --> 01:43:11,719
Ulugan and Esenbike aren't around, my Bey.

1048
01:43:11,920 --> 01:43:16,719
But the vile dog called Ilbay is in the tribe.

1049
01:43:19,680 --> 01:43:22,239
We'll burn the bales of hay...

1050
01:43:22,800 --> 01:43:25,439
...and roll towards them.

1051
01:43:25,960 --> 01:43:27,719
With Allah's will.

1052
01:43:28,480 --> 01:43:30,399
...we'll take our tribe back today.

1053
01:43:30,680 --> 01:43:32,519
God willing, my Bey.

1054
01:43:56,920 --> 01:43:58,919
Osman's coming! We're under attack!

1055
01:43:59,000 --> 01:44:02,119
Come on, attack!

1056
01:44:17,120 --> 01:44:18,679
Burn.

1057
01:44:43,680 --> 01:44:47,519
Ya Allah... Now!

1058
01:46:59,680 --> 01:47:01,639
Today is the blood day!

1059
01:47:01,800 --> 01:47:03,679
Today is the vengeance day!

1060
01:47:03,920 --> 01:47:08,839
Today, we're taking back the Kayi Tribe!

1061
01:47:10,680 --> 01:47:12,599
Ya Allah!

1062
01:47:31,440 --> 01:47:33,479
No traces this way, mother.

1063
01:47:37,800 --> 01:47:40,119
Osman must have hidden the traces.

1064
01:47:42,640 --> 01:47:45,759
It's about to get dark. What now?

1065
01:47:48,080 --> 01:47:50,919
We can never find Osman then.

1066
01:47:52,000 --> 01:47:54,359
Osman has run away for now.

1067
01:47:54,920 --> 01:47:56,999
We're going back.

1068
01:47:57,480 --> 01:48:00,039
Send a message to witch Sofia.

1069
01:48:00,360 --> 01:48:01,799
I want her to come.

1070
01:48:02,120 --> 01:48:05,879
We'll make a new plan to destroy Osman.

1071
01:48:12,840 --> 01:48:15,839
Ilbay, you're going to die today!

1072
01:48:26,240 --> 01:48:29,359
They're running away, my
Bey! Going to the headquarters!

1073
01:48:29,600 --> 01:48:31,519
Close all the gates!

1074
01:48:31,560 --> 01:48:34,479
Nobody will leave here today!

1075
01:48:54,000 --> 01:48:56,319
Come on!

1076
01:49:07,400 --> 01:49:09,079
Attack!

1077
01:50:20,200 --> 01:50:22,639
Allah is the greatest!

1078
01:50:31,640 --> 01:50:36,449
You're slower, my Bey! I thought you'd have
captured the tribe by the time I arrived.

1079
01:50:36,449 --> 01:50:38,199
I'm slower, huh?

1080
01:50:41,080 --> 01:50:45,159
-Actually you still got it.
-That's what I thought!

1081
01:51:22,640 --> 01:51:26,199
Samil, don't let that dog run away!

1082
01:51:26,560 --> 01:51:28,439
As you order, my Bey.

1083
01:51:30,640 --> 01:51:32,879
Where are you going, jackal?

1084
01:52:23,120 --> 01:52:28,239
You can't go anywhere
before you pay for your betrayal.

1085
01:52:30,840 --> 01:52:33,439
Get up. My Bey will make you pay.

1086
01:52:33,520 --> 01:52:37,279
You dog. Get up, dog!

1087
01:52:40,600 --> 01:52:42,279
Move.

1088
01:52:49,760 --> 01:52:52,799
Victory is ours!

1089
01:52:53,480 --> 01:52:56,039
Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest!

1090
01:52:56,080 --> 01:53:03,119
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

1091
01:53:03,720 --> 01:53:07,719
Allah is the greatest!

1092
01:53:07,760 --> 01:53:11,279
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah, yes.

1093
01:53:15,640 --> 01:53:17,559
Come here.

1094
01:53:23,760 --> 01:53:26,759
This dog is waiting for his death now, my Bey.

1095
01:53:40,360 --> 01:53:42,439
What kind of a Kayi are you?

1096
01:53:44,160 --> 01:53:48,799
How could you betray your own kin?

1097
01:53:50,680 --> 01:53:52,079
Speak.

1098
01:53:52,680 --> 01:53:54,399
Osman Bey.

1099
01:53:55,120 --> 01:53:58,399
He isn't my real father, Osman Bey.

1100
01:54:00,440 --> 01:54:03,439
He isn't a real Kayi either.

1101
01:54:07,360 --> 01:54:09,519
What are you talking about, Ayse?

1102
01:54:09,840 --> 01:54:11,879
I heard him talking in the tent.

1103
01:54:12,080 --> 01:54:15,359
He killed my father and took his place.

1104
01:54:15,520 --> 01:54:19,039
A real Kayi would never
do what he did, Osman Bey.

1105
01:54:29,720 --> 01:54:30,759
My daughter...

1106
01:54:33,760 --> 01:54:34,799
Come, my Ayse.

1107
01:54:34,800 --> 01:54:36,039
Kismet!

1108
01:54:36,040 --> 01:54:38,079
Ayse, go.

1109
01:54:50,080 --> 01:54:51,719
I was very close, Osman.

1110
01:54:53,480 --> 01:54:56,119
I was very close to erasing you from history.

1111
01:54:56,200 --> 01:54:57,839
You and those like you...

1112
01:54:59,360 --> 01:55:01,999
...will never be able to kill me.

1113
01:55:03,600 --> 01:55:04,639
But...

1114
01:55:06,560 --> 01:55:08,239
...you and those like you...

1115
01:55:10,320 --> 01:55:14,719
...will die by my sword of justice.

1116
01:55:39,800 --> 01:55:42,359
Another traitor got what he deserved.

1117
01:55:42,840 --> 01:55:45,239
But the other dogs are still alive.

1118
01:55:46,760 --> 01:55:48,759
Ulugan has no more days to see.

1119
01:55:50,240 --> 01:55:52,239
But Esenbike and Sargun...

1120
01:55:52,360 --> 01:55:56,399
If we kill them, we will only get in trouble.

1121
01:55:56,840 --> 01:55:58,999
We need to capture them alive.

1122
01:56:00,720 --> 01:56:02,159
If we can..

1123
01:56:02,640 --> 01:56:06,679
We will be politically superior to Olcaytu.

1124
01:56:08,200 --> 01:56:09,839
What will we do now, my Bey?

1125
01:56:13,440 --> 01:56:14,839
Lucia.

1126
01:56:15,680 --> 01:56:17,519
What did you tell Bala?

1127
01:56:18,640 --> 01:56:20,039
Who is lying?

1128
01:56:21,000 --> 01:56:22,039
You..

1129
01:56:23,480 --> 01:56:24,519
...or...

1130
01:56:25,400 --> 01:56:26,799
...my aunt?

1131
01:56:28,040 --> 01:56:29,119
Poena..

1132
01:56:31,120 --> 01:56:32,239
Poena...

1133
01:56:33,400 --> 01:56:34,719
Forgive me...

1134
01:56:37,920 --> 01:56:39,039
...I am

1135
01:56:39,840 --> 01:56:41,599
...a horrible sinner.

1136
01:56:47,600 --> 01:56:49,159
Are you playing a game with me?

1137
01:56:50,840 --> 01:56:52,479
Did Bala threaten you?

1138
01:56:53,160 --> 01:56:54,359
Poena..

1139
01:56:56,800 --> 01:56:58,039
Sofia.

1140
01:57:00,560 --> 01:57:04,839
Do not trust Sofia.

1141
01:57:05,920 --> 01:57:07,999
You united with Bala.

1142
01:57:09,120 --> 01:57:11,119
You betrayed my aunt, right?

1143
01:57:13,240 --> 01:57:15,319
That's why my aunt wanted to kill you.

1144
01:57:17,720 --> 01:57:18,839
...I did...

1145
01:57:19,760 --> 01:57:20,839
...a very...

1146
01:57:21,520 --> 01:57:22,639
...bad thing...

1147
01:57:24,560 --> 01:57:26,119
...to you.

1148
01:57:28,560 --> 01:57:29,599
Meryem.

1149
01:57:31,600 --> 01:57:32,719
Is she awake?

1150
01:57:32,720 --> 01:57:33,719
No.

1151
01:57:34,360 --> 01:57:35,799
She is not, Gonca Hatun.

1152
01:57:38,880 --> 01:57:41,039
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

1153
01:57:42,680 --> 01:57:44,239
Poena..

1154
01:57:44,880 --> 01:57:46,439
She is saying something...

1155
01:57:46,680 --> 01:57:47,839
Poena.

1156
01:57:49,520 --> 01:57:50,919
Poena..

1157
01:57:51,680 --> 01:57:53,719
Forgive me...

1158
01:57:57,560 --> 01:57:59,479
Forgive me...

1159
01:58:01,880 --> 01:58:03,039
Poena.

1160
01:58:04,720 --> 01:58:05,879
Halime's name.

1161
01:58:11,680 --> 01:58:13,519
I guess she is hallucinating

1162
01:58:13,960 --> 01:58:15,759
She has a high temperature.

1163
01:58:17,000 --> 01:58:19,559
You took our sister from us!

1164
01:58:20,440 --> 01:58:22,199
Even if she forgives you..

1165
01:58:22,440 --> 01:58:24,039
...we will not forgive you

1166
01:58:54,520 --> 01:58:55,999
Where is that Ilbay?

1167
01:58:56,000 --> 01:58:57,319
He will come here!

1168
01:59:10,120 --> 01:59:12,439
We punished that traitor.

1169
01:59:13,520 --> 01:59:15,199
We cut his head off...

1170
01:59:22,000 --> 01:59:24,079
You made a big mistake, Osman.

1171
01:59:26,000 --> 01:59:28,879
Now this war will kill you all!

1172
02:00:12,200 --> 02:00:13,399
Come on then.

1173
02:00:14,120 --> 02:00:15,639
You can all come at us!

1174
02:00:21,160 --> 02:00:22,599
Let's see..

1175
02:00:50,520 --> 02:00:51,559
Alps!

1176
02:00:55,080 --> 02:00:59,119
Allah is the Greatest!

1177
02:01:07,720 --> 02:01:09,999
Your death has come, Ulugan.

1178
02:01:10,000 --> 02:01:12,479
Who will save you from my hands, huh?

1179
02:01:15,560 --> 02:01:17,599
Attack!

1180
02:01:19,160 --> 02:01:20,719
You have a high temperature.

1181
02:01:20,960 --> 02:01:22,839
I will go and call Alaeddin Bey.

1182
02:01:23,040 --> 02:01:24,239
He will treat you.

1183
02:01:27,080 --> 02:01:28,959
...stayed silent...

1184
02:01:31,880 --> 02:01:33,559
..about..

1185
02:01:34,040 --> 02:01:35,959
...Sofia's evil plan.

1186
02:01:38,160 --> 02:01:40,519
I stayed..

1187
02:01:41,560 --> 02:01:43,439
..silent about your..

1188
02:01:45,280 --> 02:01:47,039
...separation from your family.

1189
02:01:50,000 --> 02:01:51,399
My parents are dead

1190
02:01:53,480 --> 02:01:55,239
You protected me.

1191
02:01:56,640 --> 02:02:01,039
You raised me, Lucia.

1192
02:02:01,040 --> 02:02:02,399
That's a lie.

1193
02:02:04,640 --> 02:02:07,759
Your parents are not dead.

1194
02:02:47,400 --> 02:02:51,039
Allah is the Greatest!
Allah is the Greatest!

1195
02:03:05,640 --> 02:03:08,039
Where are you going Begum, huh?

1196
02:03:08,720 --> 02:03:11,079
Did you think you would get away with it?

1197
02:03:23,480 --> 02:03:25,319
Say your final prayer, traitor.

1198
02:03:25,680 --> 02:03:27,119
Say your final prayer.

1199
02:03:30,680 --> 02:03:32,839
Her blood is halal to me, Boran Bey.

1200
02:03:33,640 --> 02:03:34,599
Stop..

1201
02:03:35,920 --> 02:03:37,759
Handle it quickly, brother.

1202
02:03:38,280 --> 02:03:39,319
Come on.

1203
02:04:18,960 --> 02:04:22,559
Allah is the Greatest!

1204
02:04:56,680 --> 02:04:59,639
Now I will cut your head off.

1205
02:04:59,800 --> 02:05:01,319
Come at me!

1206
02:05:11,760 --> 02:05:15,599
Now it's time for you to die, huh?

1207
02:05:21,760 --> 02:05:28,239
I told you I'd take a tooth for a
tooth an eye for an eye, a life for a life!

1208
02:05:28,920 --> 02:05:31,999
Come at me now...

1209
02:05:36,560 --> 02:05:37,719
Come..

1210
02:05:37,720 --> 02:05:40,279
You hurt my people!

1211
02:05:42,320 --> 02:05:45,799
You killed my innocent people!

1212
02:05:58,000 --> 02:06:00,559
So, Ulugan..

1213
02:06:02,800 --> 02:06:04,919
Now you will die.

1214
02:06:04,920 --> 02:06:08,799
You are not a state, Osman.

1215
02:06:09,120 --> 02:06:11,279
You are just a shepherd.

1216
02:06:23,280 --> 02:06:28,279
The land you step on is now my land.

1217
02:06:35,880 --> 02:06:36,919
Here..

1218
02:06:37,880 --> 02:06:41,519
l am the Bey, and I am the state!

1219
02:06:51,640 --> 02:06:55,559
Dastard dog...

1220
02:07:02,280 --> 02:07:04,439
Mother, we need to leave.

1221
02:07:04,440 --> 02:07:06,519
Our nokers died, we cannot resist now.

1222
02:07:06,680 --> 02:07:10,679
When I return here, I will make sure I
don't leave a head on their shoulders!

1223
02:07:10,680 --> 02:07:12,559
Come on, come on mother!

1224
02:07:14,440 --> 02:07:16,079
Osman took his tribe back.

1225
02:07:19,280 --> 02:07:22,079
Esenbike and his son are running away.

1226
02:07:24,320 --> 02:07:25,559
Fools.

1227
02:07:27,160 --> 02:07:30,879
They are paying the price
for letting Osman escape.

1228
02:07:31,040 --> 02:07:32,079
What will we do?

1229
02:07:33,640 --> 02:07:36,479
Osman will be stronger than before now.

1230
02:07:45,480 --> 02:07:47,919
Don't let them follow us!

1231
02:08:05,040 --> 02:08:07,759
-Come on!
-Come on!

1232
02:08:13,600 --> 02:08:15,679
Ulugan's dog!

1233
02:08:17,520 --> 02:08:18,559
Altuga...

1234
02:08:20,480 --> 02:08:23,319
Now you will pay for all the lives you took...

1235
02:08:25,000 --> 02:08:27,759
...with your own life.

1236
02:08:27,760 --> 02:08:29,839
Your owner is a corpse now.

1237
02:08:31,320 --> 02:08:32,639
Now it's your turn!

1238
02:08:34,960 --> 02:08:36,759
Angry boys...

1239
02:08:37,520 --> 02:08:39,119
Angry boys...

1240
02:08:40,640 --> 02:08:45,079
I should have hit that nail into
your forehead, not your hand.

1241
02:08:45,080 --> 02:08:47,879
I told you if you don't do it
when you have the chance...

1242
02:08:48,000 --> 02:08:53,239
...you'll regret it when you
are in my hands, Altuga, huh?

1243
02:09:38,760 --> 02:09:41,079
Altuga.

1244
02:09:42,280 --> 02:09:44,439
Osman Bey's door is open to everyone.

1245
02:09:44,720 --> 02:09:49,639
He, with Almighty Allah's order,
gives a last chance to everyone.

1246
02:09:50,760 --> 02:09:53,479
Now I am asking you for the last time, Altuga.

1247
02:09:53,800 --> 02:09:54,999
Ask for forgiveness..

1248
02:09:56,040 --> 02:09:57,599
...and choose The Righteous' way.

1249
02:10:00,160 --> 02:10:01,599
Are you serious...

1250
02:10:01,920 --> 02:10:02,959
Orhan?

1251
02:10:12,440 --> 02:10:13,559
Orhan.

1252
02:10:15,760 --> 02:10:17,559
Even if you cut my head off...

1253
02:10:17,760 --> 02:10:20,519
...I will never be your dog...

1254
02:10:20,680 --> 02:10:22,279
...like Cerkutay!

1255
02:10:22,680 --> 02:10:23,719
Never!

1256
02:10:28,760 --> 02:10:30,039
You, Altuga...

1257
02:10:31,560 --> 02:10:33,159
You chose death...

1258
02:10:34,480 --> 02:10:35,919
..not life.

1259
02:10:49,280 --> 02:10:52,519
When Cerkutay Bey hears this, he will be upset.

1260
02:10:53,640 --> 02:10:55,559
He was his brother in the end..

1261
02:10:55,840 --> 02:10:57,359
The state, Alaeddin...

1262
02:11:00,280 --> 02:11:01,639
The state never forgives.

1263
02:11:03,160 --> 02:11:04,199
Right, brother.

1264
02:11:04,640 --> 02:11:08,199
True.

1265
02:11:23,520 --> 02:11:25,119
Mother, someone's coming.

1266
02:11:33,600 --> 02:11:37,479
Esenbike!

1267
02:11:40,080 --> 02:11:41,519
I told you..

1268
02:11:43,280 --> 02:11:46,039
Whoever is above oneself
becomes the prey of Osman.

1269
02:11:46,040 --> 02:11:48,519
Now is not the day to say
meaningless words, Sofia.

1270
02:11:48,520 --> 02:11:50,719
Osman is after us.
-Don't worry...

1271
02:11:50,720 --> 02:11:52,319
I am here to save you.

1272
02:11:54,520 --> 02:11:55,559
Come on.

1273
02:11:56,400 --> 02:11:57,799
Send the horses away.

1274
02:11:58,680 --> 02:12:00,519
We'll go on foot.

1275
02:12:21,680 --> 02:12:24,319
Olcaytu will reward you for your...

1276
02:12:24,360 --> 02:12:27,039
...favour. 
-Sure he will.

1277
02:12:32,840 --> 02:12:36,559
I don't do a favour without
expecting anything in return.

1278
02:12:40,800 --> 02:12:42,839
Mother..

1279
02:13:16,480 --> 02:13:17,519
Sofia.

1280
02:13:18,200 --> 02:13:20,719
You killed Olcaytu's daughter and grandson.

1281
02:13:20,960 --> 02:13:22,159
That means death!

1282
02:13:24,320 --> 02:13:25,359
Hristo.

1283
02:13:28,440 --> 02:13:29,959
I did not kill them.

1284
02:13:31,280 --> 02:13:32,839
Osman did.

1285
02:13:36,080 --> 02:13:37,399
Hristo.

1286
02:13:38,920 --> 02:13:41,559
How could Osman make this mistake?

1287
02:13:45,160 --> 02:13:46,199
Now..

1288
02:13:48,600 --> 02:13:50,439
Olcaytu Khan...

1289
02:13:51,000 --> 02:13:52,359
...will destroy...

1290
02:13:53,120 --> 02:13:55,239
...Kayi tribe with this furor.

1291
02:13:59,600 --> 02:14:00,759
Get ready.

1292
02:14:02,680 --> 02:14:03,719
We are leaving.

1293
02:14:29,360 --> 02:14:30,399
No..

1294
02:14:31,120 --> 02:14:32,359
My parents died.

1295
02:14:34,560 --> 02:14:36,039
Bala and Osman killed them.

1296
02:14:38,040 --> 02:14:39,279
You told me!

1297
02:14:40,120 --> 02:14:41,519
You told me this, I..

1298
02:14:42,320 --> 02:14:43,799
I lived for this!

1299
02:14:47,200 --> 02:14:50,839
I lived to take our revenge from them!

1300
02:14:51,880 --> 02:14:53,759
To kill them!

1301
02:14:55,880 --> 02:14:59,519
You cannot kill them.

1302
02:15:00,640 --> 02:15:04,679
You know the truth.

1303
02:15:06,800 --> 02:15:12,399
-Sofia is your executioner...
-You are lying!

1304
02:15:13,400 --> 02:15:16,519
My aunt was right about wanting to kill you!

1305
02:15:16,960 --> 02:15:18,239
You are insane!

1306
02:15:18,760 --> 02:15:19,959
You are insane!

1307
02:15:21,000 --> 02:15:22,039
You..

1308
02:15:22,360 --> 02:15:23,759
You are a traitor!

1309
02:15:24,720 --> 02:15:26,719
Poena..

1310
02:15:27,960 --> 02:15:33,279
You were her biggest, her worst...

1311
02:15:34,160 --> 02:15:37,799
...her most merciless game.

1312
02:15:40,840 --> 02:15:47,679
She raised you to make you...

1313
02:15:48,320 --> 02:15:51,759
...kill your own family.

1314
02:15:59,920 --> 02:16:01,439
You are Osman Bey...

1315
02:16:03,080 --> 02:16:04,719
...and Bala Hatun's...

1316
02:16:06,360 --> 02:16:07,399
...daughter...

1317
02:16:07,720 --> 02:16:09,439
...Halime.

1318
02:16:11,239 --> 02:16:13,399
Forgive me.

1319
02:16:24,640 --> 02:16:26,719
No...

1320
02:16:59,600 --> 02:17:01,839
What is this, my Bey?

1321
02:17:07,920 --> 02:17:10,039
Be careful. Bala.

1322
02:17:16,480 --> 02:17:18,079
Bala.

1323
02:17:30,600 --> 02:17:32,638
She's dead.

1324
02:17:33,959 --> 02:17:35,359
She's dead.

1325
02:17:35,840 --> 02:17:39,599
Who killed them? Who else was after them?

1326
02:17:45,520 --> 02:17:49,959
The one who tries to beat
us, while we try to bring...

1327
02:17:50,280 --> 02:17:52,799
...victory and hope in these lands.

1328
02:17:54,400 --> 02:17:56,879
He's the one who killed Esenbike.

1329
02:17:57,480 --> 02:18:02,599
But if don't find out who
did this with evidence...

1330
02:18:04,719 --> 02:18:07,398
...Olcaytu's grandson and daughter...

1331
02:18:07,558 --> 02:18:12,279
Their deaths will only
bring troubles to our lands.

1332
02:18:15,400 --> 02:18:16,959
Alps.

1333
02:18:17,320 --> 02:18:19,398
Take them to our tribe.

1334
02:18:19,480 --> 02:18:21,759
Send a messenger to Olcaytu.

1335
02:18:22,600 --> 02:18:26,839
Tell them to take their funerals from our tribe.

1336
02:18:27,080 --> 02:18:28,959
As you order, my Bey.

1337
02:18:57,240 --> 02:18:59,079
My brothers.

1338
02:18:59,200 --> 02:19:00,799
Brother.

1339
02:19:11,879 --> 02:19:14,638
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah.

1340
02:19:14,799 --> 02:19:16,439
Thanks to Allah.

1341
02:19:17,920 --> 02:19:21,199
-Thanks to my Allah!
-Thanks to Allah.

1342
02:19:21,280 --> 02:19:23,439
Thanks to Allah, we took our tribe back.

1343
02:19:23,440 --> 02:19:26,159
-Thanks to Allah.
-Thanks to Allah.

1344
02:19:26,840 --> 02:19:29,279
Where are Bala Hatun and Osman Bey?

1345
02:19:31,280 --> 02:19:32,759
My Bey.

1346
02:19:32,879 --> 02:19:40,879
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

1347
02:19:41,000 --> 02:19:43,119
Thank you, thank you.

1348
02:19:43,320 --> 02:19:51,279
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

1349
02:19:51,440 --> 02:19:55,039
Mother... Father.

1350
02:19:55,320 --> 02:19:58,079
Thank you! I appreciate it.

1351
02:19:58,880 --> 02:20:00,799
My Bey.

1352
02:20:19,800 --> 02:20:23,999
Thanks to Allah, we took our home back.

1353
02:20:30,320 --> 02:20:34,119
We did. Of course, we did.

1354
02:20:40,760 --> 02:20:42,839
Thanks to my Allah!

1355
02:20:45,760 --> 02:20:48,319
We believed with no doubts...

1356
02:20:49,440 --> 02:20:52,119
...that swords drawn for Allah...

1357
02:20:53,840 --> 02:20:56,159
...always become victorious!

1358
02:20:56,680 --> 02:20:57,999
Well..

1359
02:20:59,280 --> 02:21:01,719
We cleared our tribe from heathens.

1360
02:21:02,560 --> 02:21:06,119
With Allah's will, we became victorious!

1361
02:21:08,560 --> 02:21:12,559
Yet we know our target well.

1362
02:21:13,280 --> 02:21:16,719
Until we give our last breath

1363
02:21:17,120 --> 02:21:21,199
...until we bring justice
and order in the whole world

1364
02:21:21,280 --> 02:21:22,799
...we'll never stop!

1365
02:21:22,920 --> 02:21:30,439
God willing, Osman Bey!
God willing, Osman Bey!

1366
02:21:56,320 --> 02:21:59,159
-It's time, my Bey.
-Yes, it is.

1367
02:22:00,800 --> 02:22:02,759
It is time.

1368
02:22:06,480 --> 02:22:11,319
Praise be, Praise be. Praise be.

1369
02:22:14,080 --> 02:22:17,079
O the light of my state.

1370
02:22:17,760 --> 02:22:19,599
...rise up.

1371
02:22:19,840 --> 02:22:21,599
Rise up.

1372
02:22:22,000 --> 02:22:24,039
Stand

1373
02:22:25,560 --> 02:22:30,119
The tired sun is sinking
on the horizon of the west.

1374
02:22:30,600 --> 02:22:34,439
A new hope is rising at dawn.

1375
02:22:35,400 --> 02:22:38,319
Martyrs are crying out
from the intermediate realm!

1376
02:22:38,640 --> 02:22:40,879
You've got dragged enough!

1377
02:22:41,960 --> 02:22:45,039
Go up where you belong!

1378
02:22:46,600 --> 02:22:48,799
Rise up!

1379
02:22:49,400 --> 02:22:52,679
Time for the east is passing.

1380
02:22:53,720 --> 02:22:58,119
Here rest all the lives we sacrificed.

1381
02:22:59,520 --> 02:23:02,999
Dark horses are running
without you in the steppe.

1382
02:23:03,560 --> 02:23:08,079
The wind is always asking for you.

1383
02:23:08,640 --> 02:23:10,279
Rise up.

1384
02:23:10,400 --> 02:23:13,479
Wake up to bring order in the world.

1385
02:23:14,120 --> 02:23:17,479
Stand and go up with the wind.

1386
02:23:18,280 --> 02:23:22,999
Honorable hearts expect great news from you.

1387
02:23:23,480 --> 02:23:27,759
My orphan homeland demands your shadow.

1388
02:23:28,880 --> 02:23:33,999
Hear the cry echoing in the sky.

1389
02:23:34,360 --> 02:23:36,759
Mountains and rocks...

1390
02:23:37,000 --> 02:23:40,039
Takbir! Takbir!

1391
02:23:40,760 --> 02:23:42,879
They're calling you.

1392
02:23:43,680 --> 02:23:46,639
Wipe off the rust of your thriving pride.

1393
02:23:47,040 --> 02:23:48,519
Rise up.

1394
02:23:48,760 --> 02:23:50,999
Wave for freedom.

1395
02:23:51,640 --> 02:23:54,999
Stand and go up with the wind.

1396
02:24:03,800 --> 02:24:06,279
My plane tree shall root in your shadow.

1397
02:24:06,360 --> 02:24:09,999
The call of Muhammad 
shall never stop in your dome!

1398
02:24:10,240 --> 02:24:13,679
The divine words shall
spread all around the lands.

1399
02:24:14,000 --> 02:24:16,719
The last Prophet is our guide.

1400
02:24:17,000 --> 02:24:20,399
And The Red Apple is our only path.

1401
02:24:21,259 --> 02:24:22,639
Stand up!

1402
02:24:23,120 --> 02:24:25,559
You've got dragged enough!

1403
02:24:26,195 --> 02:24:32,425
Carry the Turkish history on your shoulders,
and rise to the summit you are belong to!

1404
02:24:49,343 --> 02:24:57,873
Today is the first day of a new era.

1405
02:24:59,477 --> 02:25:04,777
O Allah.
In the name of Allah.